a series of events that were described as terroristic began , which were attributed to the forces loyal to ceausescu , which refused to recognize the new situation in the country , but most of those attacks were preempted .
ion and his front took control of the television , radio , and the rest of the media in the country , and used them for propaganda and defamation of the revolutionaries and activists .
in january 1990 , the miners ( honorable citizens ) , with the help of policemen , attacked students and intellectuals while demonstrating .
it 's worth mentioning that it was iliescu who incited the workers and policemen to carry out this attack .
let me talk about the price of the abortive revolution with respect to the number of victims .
the total number of deaths was 1 , 104 people , 162 of whom died before the deposition of ceausescu and the rest in the period of insecurity orchestrated by the national salvation front .
in romania 3 , 352 people were injured , with 1 , 107 of them being injured before the dictator was arrested ,
so we are talking about freedom that was aborted , the price of which was many deaths and injuries at the hands of those who claimed they would protect the revolution and its people .
there were 942 deaths and 2 , 245 injured people after the national salvation front grabbed the reins of all matters .
now , the romanian revolution has made the world laugh at the people of that country , who recognized that the price they paid was too high compared to what they have gained so far .
this thread is for those people who are not convinced that there is a conspiracy aiming to make the egyptians live in a situation that 's worse than what they had during the days of mubarak ,
in an interview with reuters in 2009 , cornia , one of the people who witnessed the revolution , talked about his impression of it on the day of its anniversary , saying : " disappointment . this is the word that can explain our conditions twenty years after what happened . "
people died and sacrificed their lives for freedom and the only result obtained was the well-being of the remaining people of the former regime , who continued to suppress the people and drag the whole country into the swamp of underdevelopment and failure .
finally , iliescu , the companion of the deposed dictator , was elected president in rigged elections with a majority of 85 % !
the outcome 20 years after the revolution ?
the same conditions exist as before the revolution , and even worse on economic , social and political levels , because they executed the dictator and left his faithful friend to reproduce the same regime .
note that this is documented real history , not a theory that could be right or wrong .
and for those who believe that we should end the revolution and remain silent .
it 's also for those who believe that the revolution comes as an implementation of what is called " creative chaos , " rather than allowing anger caused by the inhuman conditions that made everyone suffer to be vented .
the causes of the revolution against the dictator of romania do not need much explanation , and took the form of bad economic conditions and stupid management of resources through failed projects , and more importantly , an army of security forces controlling everything . these were heightened by accusations of treason , which affected everyone who demanded their rights and protested against the rule of a sole totalitarian party , namely the socialist party of romania .
on december 16 , 1989 , the people started a series of harsh demonstrations against the dictatorial regime in romania , which was headed by nicolas ceausescu and his wife , elena .
the demonstrations continued until dec . 22 , when ceausescu tried to escape from the presidential palace but was captured in preparation for trial on december 25 , where both he and his wife were sentenced to death by a firing squad , and the judgment was executed immediately .
after ceausescu , a new political party called " national salvation front " came to power .
this front " grew out " of the leaders of the second level of the romanian communist party , with the help of army generals .
the front 's leader was ion iliescu , a former member of the communist party and an ally of the executed dictator .
