mahmoud ghozlan , spokesman for the muslim brotherhood :
the muslim brotherhood denied making any contact with the scaf or the national forces concerning support for nabil el-arabi , secretary general of the league of arab states , as a candidate for the presidency .
mahmoud ghozlan , member of the guidance bureau and media spokesman for the muslim brotherhood , stated that posing el-arabi 's name now may be for publicity purposes , or to bring him to the focus of public attention . ghozlan explained in a statement to the al-ahram newspaper that the presidential candidate who will be supported by the muslim brotherhood will be a well-known public figure ,
because , if he depends on the votes of the brotherhood only , he will lose , adding that the brotherhood would not support a secular candidate , or any candidate who is hostile to islam . dr . abdul rahman al-barr , member of the guidance bureau and the dean of the faculty of theology and da 'wah at al azhar university in mansoura , stated that the brotherhood did not decide to support a particular candidate , and did not conduct any communications with el-arabi or pose his name for discussion ,
stressing that the brotherhood would declare the name of the candidate it supports only after closing the door to challenges in the presidential election . al-barr renewed his affirmation to al-ahram that the muslim brotherhood will not nominate any of them , or anyone from another islamic party , and that the most important conditions he should meet are integrity , nationalism and not being hostile to the muslim project .
