there was a coptic woman named fartouna who lived near the mosque . the governor of egypt , amr ibn al-as , offered to give her another house to include the area of her house in the extension of the mosque , but she refused , so he ordered that her house be demolished , and included in the mosque area , after he decided to give her another house .
the old woman became angry and traveled to medina to complain to caliph umar ibn al-khattab , who summoned amr ibn al-as immediately . when amr arrived , he explained , " oh leader of the believers , i have given her another house in exchange for hers to expand the mosque . "
umar asked , " did she agree ? , " to which he answered negatively . umar then ordered him to demolish the built part of the mosque and rebuild the house of the coptic woman at the expense of the public treasury . it 's also said that 8 coptic families were forced to leave el ameriya in 2012 .
