but dr . mahmoud ghuzlan , member of the guidance bureau , and spokesman for the " brotherhood , stated to the " al-misriyoun " newspaper : " the brotherhood didn 't discuss the matter with respect to who its candidate for the presidency will be when the door for nominations is opened on march 10 th , in order to ensure that he will be a consensual candidate that wins the support of all political forces and parties . "
he also dismissed the news , which reported that the group had decided to support nabil el-arabi , the arab league secretary general , as a candidate for the presidency , and ghuzaln stated : " nabil el-arabi 's name was not originally suggested as a candidate supported by the group . "
he also revealed that congress freedom and justice party mps will be directed to discuss the law on the election of the president of the republic issued by the supreme council of the armed forces a few days before holding parliament sessions ,
and that the new law will be re-issued if the mps deem it appropriate because the legislation and enactment of laws is the inherent jurisdiction of the parliament .
that was what actually happened when the religious committee for the people 's assembly headed by sheikh sayed askar started discussing and studying the law of the election of sheikh al-azhar , issued by the supreme council of the armed forces a few days before holding parliament sessions .
dr . ali batteekh , a member of the shura council of the brotherhood , said , " among the criteria agreed upon by the political forces are the following : the candidate shouldn 't be a military one , should be unbiased in dealing with all political forces , and should not be in conflict with any of them . another criterion is that he should not be considered if he is one of the former regime 's men . other qualities are likely to be agreed upon by the political forces . "
he explained that the planned meeting between the brotherhood and political forces would also address the discussion on the constitutional committee , so as to avoid its control by one party , and would address scheduling more meetings for political forces for greater coordination in managing the affairs of the country .
dr . mahmoud hussein , secretary general of the muslim brotherhood , stated that the conference was scheduled to be on tuesday , but some political forces sought to postpone it until the completion of the shura council elections , and did not specify any date , leaving it with an indefinite time frame .
he pointed out that all political forces were invited to attend this conference , because it would be very important , and that whoever wanted to attend would be welcomed and whoever didn 't want to attend would do so at their discretion .
in the same context , islamic parties welcomed the nomination of dr . nabil el-arabi , the secretary-general of the league of arab states , for the presidency , especially after some political forces proposed the idea of running for the elections , because he won the confidence of all parties as a consensual figure .
a member of the supreme committee of the freedom and justice party stated that nabil el-arabi is the closest candidate for presidential elections to get our support .
dr . safwat abdul-ghani , secretary general of the construction and development party , stated , " the right to run for the presidential elections is guaranteed by law and the constitution , as long as the person has the competence and ability required for this office . "
abdul-ghani added that the party had recently launched an initiative calling on all potential candidates from non-affiliates of the former regime to come to the party and present their electoral programs .
accordingly , the party will choose whomever it deems the fittest , pointing out that dr . abdel moneim aboul-fotouh came to the party on wednesday and presented his vision and his economic program . this will be followed by other meetings with all of the candidates , including dr . nabil el-arabi , who is considered a strong candidate , if he announces his official nomination .
for his part , dr . yasser abdel-tawab , communication officer for the al-nour party , stated that el-arabi won the support of the islamist parties just like the other candidates expected to be supported by them , indicating that the party was studying the programs of some candidates .
the opinion will be consensual , reflecting the agreement of all political parties and forces , and the party will not adopt any opinion that would be contrary to the opinion of the majority of political forces .
abdel-tawab pointed out that the figure who had the confidence of the majority would be the strongest in terms of the electoral program , the manner of implementing it in reality , and the manner of dealing with the problems raised on the scene .
dr . rifaat al-said , chairman of the tagammu party , welcomed el-arabi provided he officially submits his candidacy papers , pointing out , at the same time , that it was too early to choose a candidate to support in the upcoming presidential elections .
he added , " there are other candidates who haven 't appeared yet , and we should wait until they come onto the scene ; in order to choose one of them , we first need to know the final names of the candidates . we , the tagammu party , or the egyptian bloc , or the liberal forces , study the platforms of all of the candidates as well as their vision concerning the future of our country and the way in which they treat important and thorny issues . "
for his part , bilal diab , the communication coordinator for the free front for peaceful change , did not welcome the nomination of the secretary-general of the league of arab states for the presidential elections , because of the situation regarding dr . nabil with respect to syria and the arab monitoring committee . he also stated that he helped to shed more blood in syria , indicating that he was a partner in what was happening in syria , and that he belonged to the former regime .
al-misriyoun
mohamed hassan , a member of the supreme committee of the freedom and justice party , stated to the " al-misriyoun " newspaper , " el-arabi is the closest among the candidates for presidential elections to get our support . " he continued : " the party announced that it would not support the three islamic candidates : abu al-fotouh , al-awa and abu ismail .
we chose you because you 're an islamic party .
so when your choice is consensual , contrary to the will of those who elected you , we don 't need you anymore ,
because you will not be representing the people who elected you .
the party respects dr . nabil el-arabi because of his experience and work , and he is the most likely potential candidate to win the support of all the political forces . "
he added : " there are conditions that govern the election and support of the candidate , the most important of which are that he is the subject of the consensus of all of the political forces and that he works to establish the rule of law and respect for freedoms and social justice . "
hassan affirmed that his party , which represents the political arm of the muslim brotherhood , will officially announce the name of the candidate supported by the party and the brotherhood in the presidential elections , after political consensus on the likely candidate by all political forces . then it will announce the name of the candidate supported by the party , but dr . nabil el-arabi is the closest to getting our support if he runs for election .
for his turn , mahmoud amer , member of parliament and assistant secretary of the party of freedom and justice , in giza , said that the party and the muslim brotherhood would not support any of the three candidates who are considered to represent the islamic trend in the presidential elections , stressing that it was a final decision of the party .
he stated to the " al-misriyoun " newspaper that the muslim brotherhood is considering presenting a new candidate other than those already announced on the scene , but that they haven 't decided on a specific person .
he added that they were studying the matter now and would propose an appropriate name on the political forces that will meet in the conference called for by the general guide .
amer denied that the brotherhood would support dr . abdel moneim aboul-fotouh , the potential candidate for the presidency , admitting that the latter would win the support of the brotherhood youth but that this wouldn 't exceed 20 percent .
