first , i want to draw everyone 's attention to the fact that civil disobedience is a big word , which bears many meanings , and contains a lot of details and different visions .
i do not want to waste your time by writing recurrent words for or against any opinion .
instead , i want to explain and convey an important message .
civil disobedience has existed in egypt for more than sixty years ,
and just remember the rate of performance of civil servants , namely 38 minutes a day .
also , remember the police withdrawal , which caused a state of chaos that has lasted up to the present . did anyone hold them accountable for this civil disobedience ?
in addition , we have teachers who don 't explain lessons in class , and depend on private lessons and centers . isn 't this a form of civil disobedience ?
there are also nurses , doctors , and all the negative situations found in government hospitals , such as negligence , and apathy . isn 't this a form of civil disobedience ?
i just wonder about the official who was talking proudly and stating that the percentage of attendance in the ministries has reached 100 % . why didn 't he talk about the performance and development rates ?
the teacher goes to school , but doesn 't explain the lessons , relying instead on private lessons .
doctors go to work at the public hospital , but do 't work , relying instead on their private clinic .
civil servants go to work just to sign their names on the attendance sheet and leave the sheets .
female civil servants make use of their day by preparing lunch .
there are many other examples which show that without any declared civil disobedience ,
we still live surrounded by civil disobedience
and the clearest example is that of policemen .
it 's also a tacit civil disobedience .
this is the real disaster .
no one asks themselves about the reason why they don 't work .
it 's a habit which people inherited a long time ago , based on distracting the attention from accountability through idleness .
i 'll talk about my specialty , namely education , particularly the failing decisions which have caused students to disrespect teachers ,
and have caused teachers to be exposed to insults and bullying .
a student was avenging a teacher because the latter stopped him from cheating on the examinations . the student brought a gang of his friends and wanted to bully the teacher , who almost died of terror .
that teacher was a respectable senior teacher who had spent a long time in service . so what could he do in such a situation ?
the only solution is go to school then leave quickly before we are given a hard time .
