lieutenant general ahmed shafik - the likely candidate for the presidency of the republic - revealed what happened behind the scenes while ousted president hosni mubarak was making the decision to step down .
he said : that the military council did not force mubarak to step down ; rather what forced him was the revolution , pointing out that the military 's role was only to communicate the impact and the risk of these demonstrations .
he said : that the military council did not force mubarak to step down ; rather what forced him was the revolution , pointing out that the military 's role was only to communicate the size and the danger of these demonstrations .
responding to a question by " bawabat al-wafad " during his meeting with journalists during his visit to luxor yesterday evening , shafik stated that the closest candidate to him is hazem salah abu ismail ,
and he said : that he likes him a lot , justifying that by saying that his words are direct .
regarding the possibility of dropping out for the sake of abu ismail , shafik confirmed that he will not drop out for the sake of any of the candidates , and that his abandoning his candidacy would be a defeat and not dropping out .
regarding the possibility of dropping out for the sake of abu ismail , shafik confirmed that he will not drop out for the sake of any of the candidates , and that his abandoning his candidacy would be a withdrawal and not dropping out .
and regarding his opinion on amending the camp david accords , he said that we must respect what we have signed in terms of agreements , adding , " i say to all the betters , forget tampering with camp david because we cannot amend the agreement except with the agreement of all parties , especially that israel did not violate what concerns you in the agreement . "
and regarding his opinion on amending the camp david accords , he said that we must respect what we have signed in terms of agreements , adding , " i say to all the bidders , forget tampering with camp david because we cannot amend the agreement except with the agreement of all parties , especially that israel did not violate what concerns you in the agreement . "
shafik views the characteristics needed in the next president as being that he must be fair , decisive in his decisions , that he must have a vision , and that he not be a complicated person .
regarding what 's been said about replacing the el-ganzouri government with a government from the brotherhood , shafik indicated that there is no reason to dismiss the el-ganzouri government , questioning the number of those who reject the el-ganzouri government from a population of 80 million egyptians
