before we start to accuse one another of disbelief and treachery , those who object to civil disobedience may explain their concept of it , because they surely misunderstand it .
surely , the figures who support it , such as abul-fotouh and abu ismail , have certain points of view . they also enjoy credibility in this forum , and everyone loves them . these people are not traitors , liberals , or atheists , so we should think about why they support it , just as we have thought about why some people reject it .
i 'll repeat it , that the one-week holiday after the feast doesn 't cause any inactivity , and i think that if the government decides to make the easter holiday three , four , or five days , no one will object .
civil disobedience will be bad if it lasts a long time , but no one will accept that it continue for a long period .
if the scaf doesn 't respond to the demands , we will be punishing the victim rather than the wrongdoer .
concerning those who fear for our country because of civil disobedience and strikes , what would their reaction be if the government decides to give them a one-week holiday ?
of course , people would be happy to get a one-week holiday , but they reject civil disobedience because there is a difference .
during the one-week holiday , bakeries work in shifts and the electric and water facilities and some factories work even on the day of the feast .
restaurants and shops remain open .
public transit systems sometimes increase their capacity because people need to go to a lot of places during the holidays .
