statement of the muslim brotherhood group about the general strike .
with regards to the strike that we have heard about from various sources , we would like to confirm the following facts : first , we , the muslim brotherhood , are with the necessity that the people , in all their groups and categories , are positive toward the concerns and affairs of their country ,
and that they should leave behind their negativity and disinterest ,
and move to demand their public and private rights ,
and to take , in that , all legitimate and peaceful means to achieve their rights , with complete preservation of the institutions of the state .
second : that striking is a constitutional right guaranteed by the rulings of the court of cassation and assured by the international agreements that were signed by egypt ,
and this right cannot be confiscated under any pretext or justification .
third : we are for striking as a means of expression and peaceful protest in the face of the the tyrannical and oppressive practices of the executive power , which has corrupted egyptian political life and failed to deal with all life problems suffered by the egyptian citizen . .
