mp mamdouh ismail | | since the first session of the parliament , i talked with mr . el-katatni about the importance of doing the adhan in the parliament or making any hint of it .
by the way , 5 % of the mps are from cairo and giza and the rest are from other provinces ; this caused me to miss the prayer more than once .
yesterday , i reminded him of the maghrib prayer , but he sent me a piece of paper , which i still have , telling me that he would adjourn the session , but he did that 45 minutes later ; today , i was surprised that at the time for the asr prayer he didn 't adjourn the session , so i decided to put an end to this and did the adhan to remind them that the time for prayer had arrived .
finally , i was surprised when i heard the words of sheikh sayed askar , the muslim brotherhood mufti within the parliament , when he said that it was permissible to combine two prayers during work , even though allah said ,
" prayer has been prescribed on believers at fixed hours , "
and if mr . el-katatni had given me the chance to speak , i would have explained this , but he falsely accused me of making a show , which i wouldn 't accept .
