mobile phone companies announce they are prepared to assist public prosecutor 's office in unraveling the puzzle of the port said incident .
!
by yusra al-hawari . mobile phone companies have said that they are ready to assist the public prosecutor 's office in carrying out an investigation into the port said stadium incident to find the real culprits involved in the carnage that took place in the stadium during a match between al-masri and al-ahli . company sources , who wish to remain anonymous , have said that the companies are ready to release the phone records of individuals identified by the public prosecution as suspected of being involved in the incident , adding that the phone records could contribute to answering many questions about the incident . they added that they had received authorization from the public prosecution to disclose the phone logs of individuals involved in the incident since laws concerning the organization of communications prohibit companies from disclosing confidential customer records without authorization from the public prosecution . they said that the companies were ready to help the judiciary in any way possible to achieve justice and find the real criminals responsible for the port said massacre . they stated that the companies had not received any correspondence from the public prosecution to requiring the disclosure of the phone records of any of the accused , adding that the companies keep records of the numbers contacted without recording the private calls of customers since that would be illegal .
