all of the people of egypt were against mubarak and remained so until what i call " the sedition speech " that was prepared by one of mubarak 's devils to split the ranks of the revolutionaries with and begin to isolate them with his declaration that he wants to die on his land , and " some chick-pea colored talk mixed with pink like that "
and so it was , the people were divided into a number of segments ; the first was the segment benefitting from the regime and the security services , which no longer had any " occupation or business " other than the revolution , and which did not wait long before they began the counter-publicity against the revolution and " what do these people want ? the man did everything for you "
and , as a result of this , the second segment appeared quickly , and much of it was formed through watching the speech , which is a negative segment that did not go down to the street to begin with , and some of it participated , but it was participation out of experimentation ,
a participation lacking spirit , will , and desire for change
this segment was truly affected , and decided--despite the hatred of the majority of them for the rule of mubarak , of which they were the largest segment harmed--to let him finish his term and die in his country , which is a truly contradictory position ! !
as for the third segment , i belong to it and , if you are among the revolutionaries , then you surely belong to it ,
a segment that did not leave the squares and streets during the eighteen days , that was not affected by mubarak 's speech , which many of them did not hear to begin with because they were in the streets and the squares at the time , defying mubarak 's curfew , saying " there is no curfew . . let him leave first "
peace be upon you
a segment that decided to fight and learned that its going out of the square before mubarak leaves the orouba palace is virtually a death sentence against the revolutionaries and the revolution and the future of egypt or any true revolution in it if it ended in that dramatic , schemed way .
thus , the third segment is the segment that removed mubarak - even if it failed to remove his regime until now -
and it was the one that ignited the squares with the enthusiasm of the revolution ,
but has this segment diminished ? , has it disappeared ? , has it been lost ?
the truth is that this revolutionary segment remains committed and ask any one of them about his position toward the revolution , you will find him firm on what we began together , and at the utmost readiness to go down time and time again , and to sit-in , and even to revolt anew to protect the revolution ,
you will find that he knows well who is betraying the revolution ,
and has not cursed the revolution on any day ,
all the matter is that , throughout 18 days in the squares of the revolutionaries , we did not hear other than the revolutionaries or see anybody else ,
we were being stabbed in our backs on the internet and the coffeeshops - which were never devoid of their customers -
during all those days , we were feeling the spirit of the revolution and its victory because of our congregation and solidarity , but now we have begun to hear what was being said without us hearing it .
who is a revolutionary ? ?
this is , of course , in addition to the false accounts on facebook which were only a day old , and most of which were in the name of , for example , " omar , " while in the sex field , it says female , which is evidence of " stupid fabrication . "
the gist is that the revolutionary segment that insisted on change and made it is still well and has not been harmed except by some disappointment , out of its belief - - mistakenly or through what they are trying to communicate to us - - that it is an extinct class ,
and the gist is that we only need the motive to return us to the squares ,
and remember that those who have caused change have not been diminished by a single person , and that " those who did it first can do it again , o tantawi "
the revolutionary is a person who wants to change corruption to righteousness and injustice to justice and accepts nothing wrong in his life
for example : when you ride in a microbus in which there are 14 people , and you find the driver wanting to raise the fare from 50 piasters to 75 piasters , and you find most people saying " not a problem , the quarter pound . go ahead , driver , and depend on god "
but a man looks and says : " why should i pay the extra quarter pound ? "
" it is not your right to take more money , " and fights with the driver , despite that the other people are saying to him " it 's over . let 's go , man . let us see to our business "
that person is the revolutionary ; he is defending a cause that he believes in
be reassured , revolutionaries , , disappointment is an illusion , we have not been lessened by a single man
i write this blog entry as i imagine how i look , or how any revolutionary looks , sitting before his computer screen to read the comments to the revolutionary article that he published , to find that some comments--and perhaps most of them--are of the type of " may god destroy your houses , you have destroyed the country , " and " it 's over . you have been exposed and nobody listens to you anymore , " and also " shame on you . let the country calm down . "
but the revolutionaries did not do it by themselves ; the revolution did not succeed with those who were in the square alone . the revolution succeeded firstly because god wanted success for it
secondly with the sympathy of the millions with the revolutionaries and by joining them , even if by prayer , even if that is the weakest of faith
and why did they sympathize ? because they hate injustice and tyranny
then , why do the revolutionaries wish to become tyrants and steal the will of the people now , when it was they who supported them , and with whom they succeeded
