there are no mothers inside the mortuary . whenever any mother tried to get in , she would lose consciousness or lose control of herself after seeing the first two bags and was carried outside by her relatives .
there were a few fathers , most of those who could bear the situation were paternal or maternal uncles , and there were many friends inside and outside the mortuary and on the surrounding streets .
" omar died , my country , omar died in a football match , my country , " a young woman , crying as she first stepped on the street , and she went ahead , leaving behind a woman who was stumbling . i extended my hand to her and she caught me and whispered , " don 't believe her ! she must be lying , omar didn 't die , there must be some mistake . "
the hospital 's guard helped me and handed over a chair in ordr to let the woman sit down . during that time , she continued to explain to all passersby that omar had graduated two weeks ago from the american university , that the graduation ceremony would be in one week , that she asked him to get many tickets so that everyone could attend the ceremony , and that he was to join the military service in a few months .
she said that he chose to study economics and refused to study finance , as she had desired . she added , " his friends were with him in port said , and they called me and told me that he died . they must be lying , of course . "
