so far , performance is acceptable , but the problem is in the decisions . what happened yesterday is because of a political problem . unless the parliament passes decisions that address the political problem itself , they would not have succeeded in solving the problem .
but if its decisions are limited to a fact-finding commission and settling for firing the governor , the security director and a few officers , we would not be solving anything that way .
firstly , the parliament must have a role in the executive authority , either through forming a government from the parliament or receiving specific ministries such as the mass media and the interior .
secondly , accelerating the presidential elections right after the consultative council elections
thirdly , restructuring the ministry of interior within a timeframe and a well-studied reform program
fourthly , firing the attorney general and appointing a new attorney general attested to for his efficiency and integrity such as zakareya abdulaziz or ahmad mekki or other icons of independence in the judiciary
