activist ahmed salama 's testimony concerning the parliament incidents :
in brief : the muslim brotherhood received information about a plan to burn parliament , and you can see this on twitter . i won 't state the names of the people involved , to prevent some people from saying that i accused them of betrayal , but they are well-known people . the plan is on twitter and you can follow the muslim brotherhood because they are sure about the information .
the muslim brotherhood asked the ministry of interior and the military to protect parliament , but they just sent a few soldiers and officers to parliament . these were very few in number .
so , they had two choices : either go and protect parliament regardless of the insults that would be hurled at them , as is the case now , or just wait and let it burn like the scientific academy .
if you remember , khairy ramadan , supporter of the former regime , announced on air one day before the incident that the scientific academy would be burnt , but the military didn 't give a damn and let it burn before our eyes .
now the military wants to divide us into revolutionaries and members of the muslim brotherhood , to drive alone .
among the marchers were many honest people , but let 's just remember the incidents of last friday , january 27 , when we were approaching the square with marchers , including many respectable people , shouting words of protest against the military . all of a sudden , some people emerged from among the marchers and shouted insults against the muslim brotherhood , and raised their shoes and pointed with their hands in an indecent way , although the marchers were protesting against the military , not the muslim brotherhood .
what do you think ? was it better to let the parliament get burnt and have mohamed mahmoud and the cabinet incidents repeated , or protect it together as one hand ?
i personally support the " we are all khaled said " campaign ( a president is required ) and we add another demand , namely a government for national salvation made up of parliament mps , because el-ganzouri and his government sabotaged our country .
this is my point of view , which i 'd like to record .
