dr . ayman nour , founder of the revolution tomorrow party , and potential presidential candidate , predicted that january 25 th will be one of the great days of this nation in which the egyptian people will prove to be civilized , and shoulder its responsibility , and that the day will unfold safely , in a civilized manner . he also pointed out that the increase in the number of people in the square is an indicator of safety .
during a phone call to the " seven questions " show presented by journalist and writer khaled salah on el-nahar tv , he expressed his fear that unfortunate events would take place on january 29 th and the previous two days , demonstrating that large crowds require extra security . such events are more likely during the few days leading up to the 29 th , when some of the political groups were expected to hold a sit-in , to demand the achievment of the revolution 's goals , which will give deceitful people the opportunity to start violent actions .
nour also addressed a message to those whom he called ' wise people ' to deal rationally with january 25 th and the days that follow , whether we agree or disagree with the idea of a sit-in , because everyone can express his opinion , calling for the protection of what he called our sons .
he added : " egyptian blood is the red line , so we do not want to repeat the mohamed mahmoud , cabinet , or maspero incidents , because this will lead us into a new crisis , which we should avoid . "
