we won 't leave , and you can ask the people why they voted for the muslim brotherhood .
we have a main goal now , namely building a strong self-reliant state that can get rid of our subordination to other countries and practice self-determination .
the muslim brotherhood officials are well aware that now they need more consensus and not disputes .
the muslim brotherhood wants to build a means of applying sharia ' , instead of renouncing sharia .
this is the muslim brotherhood 's ideology , which made people elect them .
* the people elected them because they declared that they wanted a civil state with an islamic state in the background ( civil means not military , religious or secular ) .
* the people elected them because they had christian candidates on their roster ( which proves that they accept the other as well ) .
* the people elected them because their ideology is moderate and will suit all egyptians over the next years , and did not import any radical platform from somewhere else .
* the people elected them because they did not bury their heads in the sand one day , and did not accept isolation or alienation . rather , they continued to strive against tyrants over the years and sacrificed their money and lives . they also lost their jobs and were forced to leave their country , but did not remain silent with respect to corruption .
they always believed that only the righteous ruler was not to be revolted against , and didn 't use religion to support any ruler .
* the muslim brotherhood has engaged in politics for decades and didn 't just appear overnight , so its members know and understand its secrets and master the rules of the game .
may allah 's peace , mercy and blessings be upon you !
they have also run for elections many times and fought to win seats in parliament at a time when nomination was considered a crime , which others were afraid to face .
* they believe in democracy , multiple parties , and elections , which makes me feel reassured that as they came to power through the electoral boxes , they will also leave it the same way .
* because the muslim brotherhood has dealt with reality and has continued to grow inside and outside egypt as an organized group , they have responded to the needs of the poor in the streets and offered them aid over years .
in brief , the people did not place their trust in the brotherhood because it promised to apply shari 'a , but because they are convinced about its moderation and the method it uses in applying shari 'a .
an important note : after the referendum and the final sweeping ' yes , ' the venerable sheikh ya 'qoub stated , " the people said ' yes ' to islam , and those who do not want islam may emigrate to america or australia .
after the parliamentary elections and the brotherhood 's great success , i say that the people who said ' yes ' to the ideology of the muslim brotherhood and anyone who does not want their ideology may immigrate to saudi arabia , afghanistan , kuala lumpur , or any other country ( i 'm just kidding ; egypt is the country of all egyptians . )
a final note : i swear to allah that i am not a muslim brotherhood member and i 'm not defending it , because i have many criticisms of them , but i just admire their political ideology .
i read a lot in the past few days that people have elected the muslim brotherhood in order to apply shari 'a and that if they do not apply it , they will be considered traitors .
of course , these are strange and inappropriate things to say , because the brotherhood 's goal is not to apply sharia , and because we are not immoral people who do not want to apply sharia !
the muslim brotherhood is an islamic da 'wa ( advocacy ) group , and their basic goal is to apply allah 's law and raise the banner of islam .
the egyptian people are religious by nature , and would not accept any alternative to allah 's law .
but we are now at the beginning of empowerment after decades of rupture from the right approach .
we are now faced with external and internal challenges which reject the empowerment of a nation of " there is no god but allah and mohammed is the messenger of allah . "
the muslim brotherhood understands this very well .
the matter is not one of force or dispute .
but if we don 't set any goals we won 't achieve any progress .
a final point lies in allah 's statement , " and he who fears allah will be provided with relief and unexpected provisions by allah . " so what 's lawful is clear and what 's unlawful is also clear .
i have a question : does the muslim brotherhood guarantee that it will also win the next term ?
they announced that they would maintain all activities , including tourism , over the coming four years .
when germany was defeated and the state there fell , the germans adopted the slogan , " work or death . "
four years later , germany achieved a renaissance .
so if we set a schedule , we will at least restore egypt 's past position rather than achieve progress . this is one point .
another point lies in the fact that sheikhs don 't accept a civil state with a religious backdrop , because civil contradicts religious , just like secular knowledge contradicts religious knowledge .
sheikh wagdi ghoneim announced in an interview that it wouldn 't be correct to make egypt an islamic state .
this is the second point .
so we should set goals and work to achieve them to be on the correct path .
i think that the muslim brotherhood won the elections because of what its members offered to the people under the oppressive regime .
may allah reward them with the best and grant them success !
o . k . , nuna , congratulations to the muslim brotherhood 's victory , but we will not emigrate because this is our country and we will continue to call for applying shari 'a .
i 'm just a muslim , and i don 't belong to the muslim brotherhood or the salafists , but this doesn 't mean that i 'm against them .
