it 's ok if you want to take part in civil disobedience actions and observe the strike on february 11 th .
but do go on with the strike and refrain from eating bread prepared by an honorable baker working on that day .
it is up to you if you want to take part in a civil disobedience action and observe the strike on february 11 th !
but be consistent in your disobedience and refrain from using power at your home . this power has been provided to you thanks to honorable engineers and technicians working at power plants to light your house .
it is up to you if you want to take part in civil disobedience actions and observe the strike on february 11 th ! but do go on with your disobedience and refrain from drinking a glass of water , as it is provided to you thanks to the work of honorable technicians at water treatment plants .
it is up to you if you want to take part in civil disobedience actions and observe the strike on february 11 th , but be consistent in your disobedience and refrain from buying medicine from an honorable pharmacist who is working on that day .
it is up to you if you want to take part in civil disobedience actions and observe the strike on february 11 th , but be consistent in your disobedience and refrain from taking a taxi driven by an honorable driver working on that day .
it is up to you if you want to take part in civil disobedience actions and observe the strike on february 11 th , but be consistent in your disobedience and refrain from watching tv , as you are receiving the transmission thanks to the efforts of a host of honorable engineers and technicians working on that day .
if you are really serious about civil disobedience and striking on february 11 th , do not use the production of the labor of others .
do not buy any government product .
do not pay your utility bills for a while .
do not use government public transportation , that is , the cairo transportation agency 's buses and mini-buses .
i mean , you can go shopping today for all your needs ,
so that you do not have to , over the following couple of days , buy anything that would provide revenue for the government .
for example , you can delay payment of bills for a few days .
this will not do you any harm .
they are not going to suspend the service because of a few days ' delay .
think of it as if you were travelling away from your residence and that you will pay it when you return .
if you are going to work , do not take the bus , but rather take a microbus , a taxi , or any privately-run transportation .
hi everybody !
you are refraining from providing revenue to the government , and you are sending a message
that you refuse its passiveness , carelessness , silence , and sluggishness in responding to the blood shed , the rights wasted , and the assassins not called into account .
for those who keep on repeating that the strike will harm our economy , my reply is :
" aren 't you disturbed by the government 's reply to the people 's demand to move the ousted president to the turah prison ,
that this move would require millions to equip the hospital for his highness ? "
the prison has been holding thousands of prisoners for ages and they have never thought of upgrading it for them ,
even though many of them have had conditions that are a thousand times worse than the ousted president 's !
now they are spending millions to turn that same hospital into a seven-star suite for the ousted president ?
wouldn 't this harm the country 's economy ?
why do you accept this spending and reject the strike ?
the strike is scheduled for tomorrow february , 11 th , god willing .
aren 't you disturbed that people have to buy gas cylinders for fifty or forty pounds
when they should get it for five pounds ?
all this shit happens in the government 's view .
do you still insist upon paying your bills to a government that sells gas cylinders on the black market
while some people are killed fighting to get one ? !
aren 't you disturbed by the young men who lost their lives in the game ? their death was weird and came as result of the ministry of the interior 's negligence and recklessness ,
gates welded closed to trap the fans in ;
lights turned off so that they could not escape , and central security forces who did not intervene to break up the fights .
then , we were surprised yesterday by statements that the incident was not the result of complicity and that it is unlikely that it was the result of a plot ;
it was just football-related violence !
i have a message for those who are not convinced of the practicality of the strike , thinking that the strike is going to bring about the destruction of the country and the collapse of its economy .
as usual , a disaster is allowed to take place and then a plan is devised
so that the real culprit may not be brought to justice and may continue to carry on his business .
aren 't you disturbed that the government spent one billion pounds ( that is 1 , 00 million pounds ) on the shura council elections ;
the elections for a chamber of the parliament which we said was useless and does us no good ?
there are also the salaries and various costs after the elections .
the government , on the other hand , has ignored the suffering of pensioners and humiliates them whenever they demand a raise for their pensions .
there are many more wrongs and we all know
that they are wrong .
we should , then , reject these wrongs and take part in saying no to them .
or would you prefer to take a spectator 's position ?
striking is a statutory and constitutional right .
think .
did you take to the streets during any of the days of the revolution ?
if not , have you ever taken part in any of the million-man marches or any gathering to voice opposition to corruption , negligence , and sham trials intended to trick the people ?
if not , when are you going to take part ?
when are you going to take action and say no to oppression , corruption , and the violation of rights ?
when are you going to take an attitude of saying " enough is enough " for oppressing others ,
for corruption , for taking others ' rights lightly ,
for attacking others ,
for giving protection to criminals who kill , attack , and rob the people ?
when will you speak up ? when will you take action ? when will you take part ?
