many people believe that the turnout for the shura council elections , less than 10 % of the electorate , was due to the insignificance of the council .
however , i believe that the low turnout has exposed the actual presence of the three political currents . it has become obvious that the majority of those who voted for the muslim brotherhood , salafists and liberalists belong to the public who do not embrace their ideas ; they just trusted them to assume the responsibility . i feel that many of their voters ceased to support them when they experienced their performance at the parliament . let 's discuss this point .
