and on one of the first days of the revolution a young person approached me whose age did not exceed twenty five years and with the type of face whose features make you comfortable . he asked me : will we succeed ? so i answered him immediately : yes , definitely ! i said it while i was unsure , but we did it .
we exchanged conversation . he was a polite , intelligent and well built young man from a working class area in alexandria called " zeirbana " , which is not far from the kafr abdo ( fashionable ) area where i live , but the distance between them may be much further than it is on the ground .
he told me that he works in sharm el-sheikh , and that he spent two days on the road from sharm el-sheikh to alexandria to join revolution , and as soon as he arrived , he joined the demonstration before going to see his father and mother .
he was extremely exhausted due to the long trip which was full of checkpoints and unsafe . he spoke to me about the horrors that he saw along the way and about the prisoners who were killing and getting killed ,
he was tired and i was tired . we walked , shouted slogans , prayed , chanted , laughed , exchanged humor and ate together . we did everything like intimate friends who knew one another for years .
then it was dark , people started to leave and i had to leave to join the citizens ' committees in the district where i live .
we embraced and said goodbye with words of encouragement , him giving me strength and me giving him strength . when i left , i remembered that i had not asked him about his name and that he did not learn my name !
