from my point of view , the demands of the revolutionaries differ completely from their actions , and i am not against the revolution . on the contrary , the revolution did a lot for us , but for me , the revolution began on january 25 and ended february 11 . as for what followed , it is all official foolishness , and if this wrong someone tell me .
the demands of the revolutionaries that have been agreed upon as final are stated as follows : -
1 - we want a law state , but none of the revolutionaries would be tried for arson or damaging public and private properties .
2 - we want democracy , but anyone who objects will be considered remnants of the previous regime .
3 - we want respect for the state , but we could curse and insult all officials .
5 - we want a cultured state , but all the people since the revolution are issuing judgments about politics , law and war .
5 - we want a fair trial for mubarak and his aides , but if he does not receive a death sentence , then the judiciary must be on his side . . and we will not be quiet .
6 - we want security to return to the street , be we could hit the police and humiliate any officer and no one judges us .
7 - we want free and fair elections and the people are the ones who choose , but people should not choose islamists .
