first , that no president to be appointed can make decisions regarding the council , or in particularly the field marshall , because they believe that a civilian cannot be the supreme commander of the armed forces , so that he would not have any right to take any action with respect to the army , including of course the declaration of war , and that this decision would be limited exclusively to the commander of the armed forces
