after the friday of anger , i was crying while watching tv .
i wanted to go to tahrir , but my mom didn 't want me to .
on friday night i was standing on our terrace watching the young people who used to buy drugs in the past . they were protecting the whole street and us .
my tears flowed down when i saw them .
when the deposed president appeared on tv and announced that he would dismiss the government , i said , " thanks be to allah , we will get rid of those business people . "
but when i watched the new government , i was almost paralyzed when i saw aisha abdel-hady , who was holding a middle school certificate while she was being sworn in .
after the deposed president 's second speech , in which he said that he wanted to stay in egypt until his death , i was impressed by it a little bit .
after that , there was the interview which made us aware of the difference between one person , who was sad because of the death of our youth , and another person who was happy . it was the interview with wael ghoneim .
then it was the night which we had all waited for .
do you remember when the cia director said that mubarak would quit ?
may allah 's peace , mercy and blessings be upon you !
we waited for four hours , after which the deposed president appeared in humiliation , after his tyranny and might , and said the sentence which made my blood boil with anger , namely " i authorize the vice-president . "
finally , the last day arrived . on that day , the largest number of people gathered . remember when sheikh jibreel was weeping while praying , and we weeped too ?
remember the christians who protected the muslims while they were praying ?
it was a scene that filled our hearts with happiness .
remember how you felt when the incidents began ?
remember how you felt before the revolution ? you felt that there was no hope , didn 't you ?
allah is the greatest and everyone who had no hope should realize that allah is the greatest and egypt is fine and will be better .
