i support the revolution against oppression and corruption to the end .
because i belong to the millions of people who were harmed by the corrupt , merciless regime .
when i received an invitation to participate in the demonstrations , i felt there was no hope .
i remember this feeling well , and it was the same feeling i had during the incidents that took place in egypt .
i was wrong , because there was hope ; and i hope that there will still be hope .
i felt that we would achieve victory because allah doesn 't let down oppressed people and we were oppressed for years .
in the beginning i didn 't expect anything to happen .
i thought there were demonstrations as usual .
but i soon expected there would be a revolution , and i started to dream of a happy future , but unfortunately the revolution was a failure from my point of view .
i still feel that the revolution has been a failure and that the desired reform is unattainable .
maybe matters will become worse than they were before the revolution .
we should have hope as long as we live .
your topic inspires optimism .
people died .
stores were robbed .
on the following day , prisons were destroyed .
i became pessimistic and started to be against those people ,
and i regretted supporting them in the past .
when the army was deployed , we understood the reality of a dishonest person who corrupted our country , along with his gang .
i started to understand the reality of all political trends and discovered that i used to misunderstand many of them .
with the passage of time , i realized that what happened was the right thing , and that it should have happened long ago .
we remained silent for a long time .
i also started to go to tahrir .
i remember that there were many christians protecting our street , because we live in shoubra where a large number of christians live .
when i went there for the first time , i felt frightened when i approached the square ,
but there was a nice smell , and i felt that the souls of the people who died were there around me .
i could see their blood on the ground , even though there was no blood .
i swear by allah that i felt that their souls were there around me and were smiling at me .
now i 'm optimistic despite all that happened
egypt will improve and allah protects it .
and we will continue to be united until the day of judgment .
