making a psychologist available in all schools and at all stages ,
and to schedule a course in psychology , which can be divided into a general lesson and a private lesson .
the private one will focus on low achievers ,
and will allow a specialist to observe students ' behaviors ,
and set tests for them
according to factors that affect the student ,
such as : age , social conditions , economic conditions , and physical conditions .
this way , the specialist will be able to diagnose their problems and work to solve them .
treating them at an early age will help
and will identify students who have psychological problems , and attempt to solve these .
what do you think , fatakat members ,
i 'd like to differentiate between the role of the social worker and the psychologist , in order to know the importance of each one .
the social worker 's domain is the relationship between the child and his society ,
namely , his family , his classmates , and his relatives ,
but he / she can 't solve the child 's problems with his small society ,
such as financial problems ,
or when the child 's father decides to make the child quit school because he can 't afford to pay tuition fees ,
or when the child 's father has died , or he / she has any other financial problems which forces the child to leave school .
the social worker then can prepare a report on the child 's conditions so that school fees can be reduced .
another suggestion is to organize school trips
to familiarize the child with his country and its civilization
if we stop talking about the revolution , and about those who support it and those who don 't ,
and allow him / her find out about the beauties of his / her country , which currently is not being done .
if we imagine that seminars will be held to spread awareness among parents as to how to treat the child , [ the social worker ] can study the parents ' conditions and the possibility of their attendance at the seminars on the educational bases , as well as their degree of understanding of such seminars , and find solutions to attract them to such seminars .
so his / her role covers the relationship between the student and his small society in an attempt to change the external conditions that affect the student negatively , without probing into the student 's psychological conditions .
this is undoubtedly a great role .
but there is a role that he / she should complete ;
namely , the role of the psychologist .
this involves observing the problems experienced by the student .
some examples are : a child who is well off and
who is a low-achiever ;
aggressive or stubborn children ;
as well as about those who think it is right and those who think it is wrong ?
a child who memorizes lessons without understanding ;
or any other psychological problem that may affect the child .
he / she [ the psychologist ] is usually the first one to notice the beginnings of the problem through the psychology lesson .
by conducting several interviews , he / she can identify the problem
and begin to solve it by shaping the student 's thinking .
we might be able to assume that the student is imitating the aggressive behavior of his / her parents ,
or any wrong behavior which he / she learned from the parents ,
or even from a person who serves as his / her role model .
the psychologist can show him a good example ,
and change the course of the student 's thinking and behavior properly , without beating and insulting
what if we were to prepare a topic which presents all our proposals for the development of egypt in all fields ,
and without using any other negative methods , such as those possibly adopted by the parents , which affect the student 's behavior .
and if the child is depressed , as a result of the death or separation of his parents ,
the psychologist can explain to the student the matters that the child can 't understand due to his young age ,
thus saving him / her from problems and preparing him / her to change the behavior .
so the role of the psychologist is that of a filter that rids the child of his problems and suffering ,
and directs him / her down the right path and attracts his / her attention to creativity .
thus , we can help the child stay away from problems .
the psychologist helps the child formulate a plan to achieve a particular goal , and helps him go on his way to reach the goal .
thus we can contribute to the existence of high achievers .
i also suggest that the psychologist undertake the following : -
based on the fact that we are the youth , and we are concerned about egypt and wish to make it the best country in the world ?
providing toys which represent the different professions
and objects which help develop innovation .
the psychologist should observe children
to know the tendencies of each child and identify creative children ,
so that he / she can develop within the student a love for a profession
and help him / her discover more information about it .
in the end , the child will achieve his goal
and won 't be exposed to disappointment at the beginning of his life .
this will produce an optimistic young person who has set his goal early in his childhood and works to achieve it .
this will allow us to get rid of the secondary school general certificate ,
so let 's make suggestions and present ideas that can help our country achieve development in all fields .
but will depend on the person 's abilities , interests and tendencies .
so if we pay attention to the psychological aspect of the child 's development starting in early childhood ,
education will improve a great deal , because it won 't be based on memorizing
and students will not be forced to join a certain faculty
without benefiting from their studies at the secondary level ,
and maybe they can 't benefit from their studies in their professional lives .
this way , the child will love a certain profession without the interference of his / her parents , who may make him enter one which he doesn 't like .
he / she will also want to learn it and take it as his / her career .
it 's also better to offer training in different professions in the advanced educational stages , such as university .
