signature : a simple egyptian citizen who lived through the revolution of july and january
1 - the july revolution was conducted by a limited group that can be counted on the fingers of the hand , by officers who called themselves the free officers , and was in the form of a military coup , whereas the youth revolution was a popular revolution carried out by hundreds of thousands of the youth
2 - the july revolution 's leaders had limited education but revolted against the regime . the youth revolution 's leaders were intellectuals revolting against the regime .
3 - the july revolution was against foreign occupation . the youth revolution was against a national occupation .
4 - the july revolution was against monarchy and hereditary rule . the youth revolution was against the republic and hereditary rule .
5 - the july revolution did not meet with resistance because the king rejected the spilling of egyptian blood and took the initiative to leave . the youth revolution faced the most atrocious instruments and methods of suppression because the president preferred to spill blood in order to remain in power for life and to pass rule on to his son .
the july revolution destroyed a semi-real democracy and strong parties and brought dictatorial rule by ignorant officers who assumed ministerial positions . the youth revolution destroyed an illusory democracy and canned cartoon parties , and is seeking true democracy and specialized ministers ( technocrats ) .
the july revolution wasted the resources of egypt in losing wars and did not seek any development . the youth revolution is trying to create a new egyptian person who seeks to develop his country .
the july revolution concentrated on spreading strife between muslims and christians in order to weaken the unity of the people . the youth revolution is concentrating on a complete dissolution and warmth between the two elements of the nation .
a greeting to our great army that carried out the july revolution . it was my hope that in the january revolution it would do what it did in the july revolution : confiscate money and property , banish the king , and swiftly try all the traitors . i didn 't want it to protect the revolution ; i wanted it to adopt the revolution and achieve its demands without us thinking or demanding . i hoped
