the coalition of the 25 january revolution in qena declares a boycott of the presidential candidate amr moussa
the coalition of the 25 january revolution in the governorate of qena issued a statement boycotting the conference of amr moussa , a candidate for president of the republic .
mohammad al faddar , member of the coalition of the revolution in qena - in a statement on friday - said : we call for boycotting amr moussa the presidential candidate because we have ideological differences with him , since during his tenure in the league of arab states he did not fulfill the desired wishes of the arab people
and the arab league did not appear with strength during the events of gaza , iraq , yemen , libya , and syria when he was assuming the position of a general secretary of the league of arab states .
al-faddar indicated that amr moussa glorified the arab leaders and described them with qualities which they do not have , for example , he described qaddafi as the premier arab leader , the leader of leaders , and the king of africa . also he did not declare his attitude toward the palestinian cause and the 25 january revolution only at a late time .
he also said that the presidential candidate did not discuss the crisis which the governorate of qena went through although he was present in the governorates of upper egypt and did not participate in this issue . he also organized his conference which was held in qena yesterday , thursday evening in collaboration with the remnants of the national party who do not express the will of the people of qena .
he also said that members of the revolution coalition distributed several leaflets during the conference , some which said : " no for he who said that gamal is a clever and efficient young man . no , for he who said that he would vote for mubarak if he runs for presidency and that he trusts his management and does not agree on him being tried . " quoted from egynews
