third , there is the spirit of the ship , which requires that none of us think that he can survive alone and leave the others to make holes in the bottom of the ship without caring about the general interest .
because it is one ship for all of us . we do not allow anyone to hijack it , make holes in it , or jump from it , because when the sun rises , it rises on everyone .
fourth , there is the spirit of the sapling , which we are ordered to plant , even if the day of judgment was in another moment / hour ,
because the responsibility for reform is permanent and continuous , even if we do not see its benefits in our lifetime .
and perhaps that was the spirit that prevailed over everyone who participated in the revolution of january 25 th , because everyone gave what he could of his time , his money , and his blood until we were ready to stand up . . so we did .
and fifth , the spirit of the frontier , which means that each one of us is responsible for a frontier of reform , everyone regardless of his position and his field ,
and fifth , the spirit of the frontier , which means that each one of us is responsible for a frontier of reform , everyone in his position and his field ,
everyone needs to work hard and think about how he can reform what 's under his control before he thinks about reforming what is far from his sphere of influence .
these are five weapons that we need in five battles we are losing : the domain of personal morals ( when was the last time you acted based on your conscience and not interests ? )
these are five weapons that we need in five battles we lagging behind in : the domain of personal morals ( when was the last time you acted based on your conscience and not interests ? )
the domain of public morals ( when was the last time you did not cut in line ? )
the domain of public morals ( when was the last time you respected any line ? )
the domain of education and awareness ( when was the last time you tried to educate a friend regarding his political obligations ? )
to the youth i speak , in response to some of their letters and their questions regarding their role that they want to play without them knowing whether they are qualified for it or not .
the domain of involvement and volunteering ( when was the last time you volunteered to do community work ? )
and the domain of wise governance ( when was the last time you attended a political forum to learn what you don 't know about the nation 's affairs ? )
the challenges are many , and the spirit of reform is the greatest thing we came out with from our revolution , so let 's invest in it .
