the swiss foreign ministry announced today , monday , that switzerland found 360 million swiss francs ( 41 , 508 million dollars ) deposited in its banks that might be unlawful assets related to the libyan leader muammar gaddafi and his entourage .
the state department spokesman , lars notchel , said that transactions related to a sum amounting to about 410 million swiss francs were tracked . its relation to the former egyptian president hosni mubarak was traced .
also an amount of 60 million swiss francs related to the former tunisian president , zin el abidine bin ali .
notchel added to reuters : " in the case of libya , the amount was 360 million swiss francs " .
these amounts were frozen in switzerland after the swiss government issued orders to prevent the disposition of assets that might be unlawful in switzerland .
the source : shourok newspaper website and hundreds of other news sites and newspapers
