the place was elegant and grand , with all means of comfort : a refrigerator , large screen television and laptop .
there was a comfortable sofa and plush seats for visitors .
the wall opposite the bed was empty , and against it were pots of nice shade plants .
the light was low , and the former president could have increased the light through a small dial affixed in the wall , but he felt comfortable in the dark .
a state of satisfaction washed over mubarak and he thought that the doctors and nurses at the hospital treat him with love and respect .
he said to himself : " those represent the majority of the egyptians who still love me and admit my favors to the country . . contrary to the suspicious elements that participated in the demonstrations on january 25 . .
all those demonstrators are agents of foreign parties that want to destroy the homeland . they have spread chaos and called it a revolution . .
they now want to put me on trial . . welcome . . go ahead put me on trial . . try to find any account or property in my name . . " .
they now want to put me on trial . . welcome . . go ahead put me on trial . . if you 're good to find any account or property in my name . . " .
the president sunk in his bed , stretched his hands , folded them on his stomach and stared at the ceiling .
this was his habit before falling asleep .
once the former president hosni mubarak felt pain in his chest , he was immediately transferred to the presidential suite at sharm el-sheikh international hospital
gradually he started to close his eyes , but suddenly he became alert to something strange :
blue lights circulating in the place as if emanating from flashlights moving in every direction .
mubarak sat up straight and kept staring at the moving lights in shock .
suddenly he heard a strange voice reverberating strongly : - hosni mubarak
mubarak looked around him but couldn 't find the source of the voice that came back to say : - you will only hear me but you will not see me .
mubarak jerked . he reached his hand and pressed the buzzer to call the nurse , but he found the buzzer not working . here the voice warned : - don 't call for help , no one will help you .
fear was etched on mubarak 's face , he looked up and said in a gravelly voice . who are you and what do you want . . ?
who am i is not important . i came to talk to you about the trial you will undergo .
- i 'm ready for the trial , i trust in the justice of the judiciary that will acquit me .
- you are of course confident after your american attorney affirmed to you that he had disposed of all the bank accounts registered in your name abroad . .
there , he had all the necessary scans and texts , which revealed a minor circulatory disorder that the doctors succeeded in controlling . .
i don 't allow you .
that is what mubarak shouted , but the voice said :
- calm down and lower your voice . . you will not be on trial only for the looted money .
you were not the manager of a bank , you were egypt 's president for thirty years , during which you took your country to the lowest abyss in all fields .
mubarak seemed ready to pounce and said angrily : - the achievements i have realized for egypt the entire world attests to .
laughter reverberated in the place and then the voice said : - i came today to review with you some of your great achievements .
i have prepared a special presentation for you that you will watch alone . look there . look .
the opposite wall had turned to what looked like a luminescent screen on which appeared many faces close together ,
they were all faces of boys and girls , children not older than ten years . .
they had different features but they were all looking deeply into the distance as if they could see something we couldn 't .
at around seven in the evening , the hospital director checked the former president again , his face showed reassurance and said while removing the stethoscope away from his ears : - praise god your health is perfect . all you need is a day or two of rest .
their faces were very pale , and many of them the hair has fallen off their tiny heads that seemed bold . .
their appearance a cause for dread and doom . . the voice said sadly : - this is a sample from thousands of children who suffered from cancer in you era as a result of the carcinogenic foods your followers used to import for the egyptian people to eat .
mubarak mumbled saying : - i 'm not responsible for this .
- are you still petulant . . ? don 't you know who imported the carcinogenic pesticides and who protected them from punishment . . ?
mubarak looked away in disgust as if saying i will not respond to this talk . .
the voice said : - look now again , the scene has changed .
instead of the faces of the sick children , many faces of men and women appeared , their bodies were bloated and their faces were blue and swollen , and their eyes carried a cold fixed look like that of the dead . . the voice said : - those are some of the people who drowned in the catastrophe of el-salam ferry 98 . . the ferry of death . . do you remember them . . ? !
- i didn 't cause their death .
- no , you 're the cause of all their tragedies . .
those are people whose country couldn 't accommodate them as a result of your injustice and corruption , so they left to work in the gulf , where they suffered from insults and humiliation , and when they returned your regime caused them to drown . .
president mubarak nodded his head and said : thank you doctor .
i think you know who the owner of the ferry is , who his partners are , and where he is now . .
when the families of those victims demonstrated to get the bodies of their families out of the sea the central security soldiers beat them up viciously .
- it 's tragic .
- the tragic thing is that you didn 't feel the depth of the tragedy , and instead of going to meet the families of the victims , you went to attend the training of the national soccer team and exchanged jokes with the players , without the slightest respect for the sorrow of the families of the victims . .
you even have a recorded video in which you make fun of the death ferry catastrophe and laugh from your heart as if those who died were not human beings .
hosni mubarak fell silent and then said : excuse me , i want to sleep .
- you must see the full presentation . . look .
the scene on the wall had changed and was showing the bodies of naked me , hanging by their feet like slaughtered animals , and on their backs the scars of severe beating . . the voice said : - these are only a sample of tens of thousands who were horribly tortured at the state security police . .
look to the right . there . mubarak looked and saw a group of soldiers attempting to undress a woman .
the woman fought desperately and kept screaming , but the soldiers overcame her and tore her clothes off till she was completely naked .
the doctor bent down and whispered respectfully : - i will leave you now to sleep and will see you in the morning -
hosni mubarak swallowed and the voice said in a moved tone : - this is what the state security police did in your time . .
they rape a woman in front of her husband to break his manhood and force him to admit what they want .
mubarak fell silent again , as if realizing that there is no use for his objections . . the voice came back to say : - look . . this is the last of you great achievements .
the pictures of the torture victims disappeared from the wall and in their place appeared the faces of tens of young men and women , all in their twenties . their heads and chests were riddled with bullets . .
the strange thing is that they all had one expression on their faces . a calm and secure expression , as it it 's contentment . as if it 's satisfaction . as if they have done their duty and are relieved . . the voice said : - you are the first president of egypt to kill egyptians with live bullets , and the first president to use sharpshooters against his own people .
all these are your victims in the revolution . . 1400 egyptians lost their eyes from rubber bullets
and the number of martyrs is close to a thousand . there are thousands missing and we will discover that many of them have been martyred . .
these are your achievements .
mubarak remained silent but the voice said : - i just want you to put yourself in the place of the mother of any martyr .
think of how she was happy with her son and her effort in raising him up , seeing him growing older one year at a time , and she was proud of him as he finished his education .
i 'm staying up tonight and there are two nurses at your call . if you want anything press the button .
remember the happy future she dreamt for him . but you killed him to remain in power and for your son to inherit it .
- shut up .
- this is a fact .
mubarak seemed to have lost his self control so he yelled :
- even if i had erred , i fought to defend egypt .
- you served your duty in the armed forces , nothing more and nothing less ,
this cannot make us forgive all the crimes you 've committed over thirty years . .
and you we not the only one who fought . thousands of officers and soldiers fought with you , and many of them performed better than you . .
do you remember lieutenant general saad el-din el-shazly . . ?
i will not respond to you .
the director excused himself and left . .
lieutenant general el-shazly was a national hero , he was the commander in chief , and the mastermind of the " high minarets " plan that was carried out by the army in the 73 war and let to its victory .
