the new national " submits its establishment documents to the parties committee next week "
saeid el-far , former leader at the national party revealed that a number of former party leaders who were known for integrity during his membership at the national party , and whose reputations were not marred by any corruption have started to establish a new party that is called as yet the " new national " .
in his statement to " al-yom al-sabe ' " el-far explained that talaat sadat , the former president of the national party will be its current president , in order to move out from under the corruption cloak of the former national party .
in his statement to " the seventh day " el-far explained that talaat sadat , the former president of the national party will be its current president , in order to move out from under the corruption cloak of the former national party .
el-far stressed that the new party will set strict regulations to limit the participation or inclusion of any of the former party leaderships that were accused in any of the corruption crimes that caused the death of the political life in egypt .
el-far added that the leaderships of the party have started to intensify their meetings to complete the documents for founding the party within this week , and complete the party charter which allows youth the opportunity to occupy leadership posts , in addition to its objectives which emanate from the demands of the revolution .
el-far also revealed that he had submitted the papers of the new party to the parties affairs committee next week in his capacity as the representative of the party founders , so that the new party would see the light of freedom to express the demands of the egyptian people .
