tens of women , children , and the elderly organized very funny demonstrations at moustafa mahmoud square in mohandessin , demanding the return of the former president hosni mubarak , and in fact , the wit was not in their request , as it is their right regardless of the merits of accepting or rejecting it .
but the interesting , even the surprising , point in the motives that led them to express their desire for the return of the ousted president . when we discussed with one of the female demonstrators the reason for demanding the return of the president and for joining this demonstration , she answered spontaneously : " sinai will be lost from us if the president didn 't return to rule egypt ,
" sir , they want to abolish the sinai liberation day " .
another elderly man carried the photograph of the president and held it close to his chest , he said that he was going on his way when some people stopped him , gave him twenty pounds and asked him to stand in the demonstration .
another girl hid her face behind a photograph of the president and refused to comment on the reason for joining the return demonstration .
other citizens also demonstrated in front of the radio and television building " maspero " to express their objection to questioning the former president .
the demonstrators objecting to questioning mubarak also raised banners denouncing the decision to imprison him for 15 days pending investigations , they also raised photographs and slogans in support of him , and took the corniche sidewalk opposite the building as the place for their demonstration .
