human rights activist saly samy - from amnesty international - and human rights activist and blogger amr gharbiyyah provided much support and advice to mansour .
al-jazeera talk show learned from special sources that activist wael ghuneim mentioned in his meeting with the leaders of the armed forces that there is another person who participated in developing the we are all khalid said page but he did not mention his name because he was waiting for the right time .
abdel rahman mansour is a recent graduate of the college of arts , mansoura university , and he is a young egyptian activist and blogger .
during his studies he worked as a correspondent to several websites including " al-jazeera talk show " which is aimed at young people .
before mubarak stepped down and the revolution was victorious , some lies and rumors were spread through the official media about the character of the moderator of the we are all khalid said page although everyone was careful not to mention their names out of faithfulness to the idea and the purpose for which the page was created .
it is said that the we are all khalid said page was created after the killing of young man named khalid said at the hands of egyptian police men in alexandria as a result of torture
the page set off several protests against torture and other issues
before the egyptian revolution started the page had almost half a million participants
the number is now about one million making it the biggest human rights group on facebook . .
nb : al-jazeera talk show is a forum like any other forum , which means that it is neither a bad or obscene thing
mona el shazly 's episode with the armed forces
hopefully after he comes back on leave and shows up to meetings , abdel rahman will not be said to be bourgeois
the episode is divided into 8 parts for easy downloading and watching
and for the difficulty of uploading
activists revealed to al-jazeera talk show that the admin ( moderator ) of the page we are all khaled said the one who set off the revolution is abdel rahman mansour and wael ghuneim .
the first one started his military service one week before the revolution broke out . so his friends made his name invisible for fear that he would be attacked especially after wael ghuneim was arrested .
activists now wait for the return of mansour on leave very soon . . after a long period of absence .
activist and blogger ahmad saleh as well as activist and blogger amr magdy , correspondent of al-jazeera talk show , in addition to other sources confirmed that abdel rahman mansour was the one who called for the 25 january demonstrations on the page before he stopped his activities to join the army .
and that he was the main motivator of the page along with activist wael ghuneim who was arrested for several days during the revolution .
activist ahmad saleh and activist nabil abdel wahhab had supported the page during the absence of abdel rahman mansour while he was serving in the military and while wael ghuneim was in detention .
