the lawyer mohiy mohammad rashed , the one who filed the case to invalidate former president mohammad hosni mubarak 's decision to step down , demanded that the commander of the presidential guard protect mubarak and respect the loyalty oath and constitutional legitimacy and respect the law , as indicated by his statement no . 4 entitled , " the fourth statement of egypt 's free lawyer . "
in his statement , rashed asked the public prosecution , counsel dr . abdul majid mahmoud , the public prosecutor , to disclose which law the former president mubarak will be tried under and to declare this in front of the public .
the lawyer also said in his statement : " based on our belief in respect for the constitution and the law , and based on the section on the legal profession in article 20 of law no . 17 of 1983 , which states , " i swear by almighty god to practice the legal profession with honor , integrity and independence , and to preserve the secrets and traditions of the legal profession and to respect the constitution and the law , " and based on our belief in respect for this oath and respect for the constitution and the law , we have filed this case before the council of state because the president 's decision has violated the constitution and the law .
rashed further said in the statement , of which masrawi received a copy : " based on our belief that freedom of opinion is guaranteed and that each person may express his opinion and disseminate it through speech , writing , or copying , or any other means of expression within the limits of the law , self-criticism , and constructive criticism to ensure the soundness the national fabric according to article 47 of the constitution , every respectable journalist or media professional should not be a " stooge . " if people do good he does good , and if they do bad he does bad , therefore , so he needs to accustom himself to doing good in words and deeds , following the role model of god 's messenger . "
he continued : " each journalist or media professional who attacks mr . president verbally or in action should respect himself , the constitution , and the law .
