a part of the stance by the supporters of former president hosni mubarak
tens of young people organized a stance in support of former president mohamed hosni mubarak this evening at moustafa mahmoud square following the recorded statement he gave on al arabiya channel .
participating in the stance was a group of national powers opposing the former president , and they denounced what was happening on the part of the egyptian youth in tahrir square and their constant appeal to put the former president on trial and subpoenaing him for questioning in a way that doesn 't befit the president of the republic of egypt .
the supporters stressed that they were not against the law or questioning mubarak " but this should be done in a befitting way as a president in egypt 's history and an october war hero , without humiliating him or touching on his pride " .
the supporters sent a message to those holding a sit-in at tahrir square saying " we didn 't and will not hold back from defending and sacrificing our lives and blood for the former president mubarak " .
karim hussein , founder of " i 'm sorry president " page on facebook told the " seventh day " that the period lived by the egyptian people have become black after mubarak 's decision to step down from the presidency , and stressed that their demands are moral and are not in conflict with the law or legitimacy , so if not in respect for his military history , it is in respect for his age and health condition .
karim hussein , founder of " i 'm sorry president " page on facebook told the " al-yom al-sabe ' " that the period lived by the egyptian people have become black after mubarak 's decision to step down from the presidency , and stressed that their demands are moral and are not in conflict with the law or legitimacy , so if not in respect for his military history , it is in respect for his age and health condition .
the supporters announced to the " seventh day " their continued support in moustafa mahmoud square daily from twelve noon till the curfew ,
the supporters announced to the " al-yom al-sabe ' " their continued support in moustafa mahmoud square daily from twelve noon till the curfew ,
they also announced organizing what they called the " people 's uprising " on sinai liberation day on the next april twenty fifth , which will be launched from moustafa mahmoud square to maspero to restore the dignity of the former president , the hero of october war as they said .
the supporters chanted slogans " o tahrir o tahrir the president has always been big " , " o mubarak o pilot , we have come for restitution " , and " the president has a palace and will live and die in egypt " , they also raised photos of president mubarak .
