the division of parliamentary editors held a big celebration in honor of the parliamentary symbols of the current 2005 - 2010 legislative session at the conference hall in nasr city . the division decided to grant dr . ahmed fathi sorour , speaker of the people 's assembly , the shield of legislative excellence for his role in passing legislation pertaining to political and democratic reform during the era of president mohamed hosni mubarak .
the division has also decided to choose safwat al-sherif , head of the shura council , as the best head of the council since its inception in 1980 and his important role in highlighting the political and legislative performance of the council . he was granted the shield of democratic excellence .
the division has chosen dr . zakaria azmi as the best member of this legislative session for his national role , commitment to respect for the constitution and his desire to protect the people 's interests . he was granted the shield of parliamentary excellence .
also ahmed ezz , head of the plan and budget committee , won second place . mohamed abul-enein was chosen as the best head of a committee and best euro-mediterranean parliamentary diplomacy representative . they were granted the shield of parliamentary excellence .
50 members , of whom 38 were from the national democratic party and 12 from the opposition , were also honored . likewise , kamal el-shazly was honored and granted the shield of excellence for being the best minister and parliamentary member throughout his lifetime and for being the oldest parliamentary member in the world . three other members were exemplary for their parliamentary performance and giving , namely : sayed rustom , el-refaie hamada and khaled zrdq .
