i was astounded . i stood there unable to speak , with my mouth wide open
then , i followed the newscast images showing ayman nour with his supporters celebrating victory and the new president , ayman nour , giving a statement
astonished , i went to the window and opened it quickly . i found the sun shining as usual . i found people walking in the street and life going on normally . ( i 'll go crazy )
i followed the rest of the news , such as " people in cairo in rapture with end of mubarak era , " " celebrations for ayman nour victory , " " amazement in the streets ; some people in disbelief , saying it 's a trick " , " citizen struck dumb with joy "
but , regrettably , i couldn 't continue my dream , because a policeman , who was standing before the committee so he could perform his role with the utmost efficiency , stared at me and said , " why are you standing here ? come on , you cannot stand here "
i left but i was still thinking about the issue . then i met my friend at night . he asked : " do you still think that ayman nour may win the election ? "
so , i answered his question with another question : " can you imagine waking up tomorrow to find someone other than president mubarak ruling egypt ? "
without exaggeration , the idea of someone other than president mubarak ruling egypt has become strange and odd , and inspires horror , astonishment , and sometimes , diarrhea . this is due to the long period of president mubarak 's being in power
changing the president of the republic is very normal and natural in many countries of the world , even if he is loved by the people . but here it has come to be an incredible myth
i was born with president mubarak ruling egypt . i 'm now thirty years old and still president mubarak is ruling egypt
i was born in 1980 , so of course i didn 't see president sadat
i would like to see another president before i die
i grew up with president mubarak in power . it 's as if he 's something eternal , like the sun rising in the east , or death . ( choose which simile suits you best )
i remember the days of the previous elections when clause 76 of the constitution was amended to make the president elected by secret ballot instead of referendum , allowing others to run against the president of the republic
on election day , i went to one of the committees near my home and i saw voters coming to vote . i stood before the committee and started to dream
i dreamt that i woke up the day after the presidential elections . i turned on the tv to al-jazeera to find the news announcing the victory of dr . ayman nour in the presidential elections
( why ayman nour in particular ? because he was the closest of the candidates )
i couldn 't believe it . is this possible ? will egypt be ruled by someone other than president mubarak ?
quickly , i started to search the egyptian tv channels to confirm the news
i must confirm such news , especially since we all know instinctively that al-jazeera is " bad and doesn 't like egypt . " then i saw the egyptian channels announcing the news that dr . ayman nour won by a slim majority against the candidate hosni mubarak
