the camp david accords is an agreement signed on september 17 , 1978 between the late egyptian president , anwar sadat , and the late israeli prime minister , menachem begin . the accords were signed after 12 days of negotiations at the presidential retreat camp david in maryland , near the capital of the united states , washington
the negotiations and signing of the accords were under the supervision of the former u . s . president , jimmy carter . as a result of these accords , the policies of a number of arab states towards egypt changed due to what was described by some as sadat 's signature on the peace agreement without demanding " concessions " on the israeli side
without demanding israeli 's recognition of the palestinian people 's right to self-determination . egypt 's membership in the league of arab states was suspended from 1979 to 1989 as a result of signing these accords . on the other hand , the two leaders jointly won the nobel peace prize in 1978 after the accords , according to the justification for the prize grant , " for the tireless efforts to achieve peace in the middle east . "
