dr . amr hamzawy denied rumors that he said that a female muslim is entitled to marry a christian , which was published on al-ahram 's main portal . it is said that during the press conference held today , hamzawy kicked out a journalist following an altercation between them .
hamzawy said in his statement : i never called for the marriage of a female muslim to a christian , and didn 't promote the violation of the provisions of shariah law . i only aimed at two phrases , and within the context of demonstrating the importance of mixing between religious laws and man-made laws in a civil state .
i demonstrated this through civil marriage as a choice and practice available to citizens within limits that don 't violate religious laws . the truth also is that the laws in force in egypt today allow civil marriage in this sense in the case of egyptians marrying foreigners or a second marriage for copts .
still , there are many attempts to drag me into a situation that contradicts shariah , claiming that i 'm calling for the violation of provisions of islamic shariah law , and alleging that liberalism is nothing but violation of religion . however , this is not true and is totally rejected .
hamzawy added : perhaps i didn 't succeed during the interview with amr adib in formulating in clear language civil marriage that complies with provisions of shariah . however , i don 't know why my phrases were decontextualized and removed from the focus of the discussion between me and adib around democracy , civil liberty , and rights , and a liberalism that defends freedom kept in check by the public interest .
why was it opened to public opinion in such a shocking way that gave rise to suspicions around me from some of my observers regarding my real position and that of liberal currents toward religion ?
hamzawy noted that he responded and gave a full clarification of his position in the following episode of the same . program , and he also wrote an explanation in his column in the newspaper " shorouk . " however , those who aim to distort are not looking for the truth as much as they 're looking for fragmented segments to serve their purposes .
