dear reader , perhaps you might be asking what i am hinting at behind my topic . and what am i hinting at with stressing the non-peaceful revolution ?
this is what i 'll answer to the second part of my topic . so , follow me .
perhaps if we stopped at the lessons first learned from the arab revolutions , we 'll necessarily reach an inevitable result that nobody could deny or deviate from . this result is the complete failure of peaceful means and methods in removing repressive compulsory regimes .
everybody who sought to remove these regimes through peaceful means , whether he was liberal or religious , must confess that he was wrong in thinking once about the possibility of changing these regimes with peaceful methods .
there 's an important matter that must be clarified to the kind reader to prove the validity of my speech .
namely , that all countries whose natives are still adhering to the peaceful revolution on their side only , didn 't achieve the change they hoped for , and their president didn 't depart . this confirms the inevitability of bloody armed confrontations .
so that nobody would hastily mention the two egyptian and tunisian examples as evidence of their rulers ' departure without the people 's recourse to arms .
i say that the tunisian president didn 't depart except after the people besieged the presidential palace . this indicates that violence was imminent . nothing remained but one treacherous bullet coming from the rifle of one the palace 's guards and the matter would turn to a fierce disorder that could have ended up in storming the palace and killing whoever was inside .
similarly , the egyptian president didn 't announce stepping down except after the revolutionists threatened to go to al-ouruba palace . they even started to move towards the presidential palace a short while before announcing stepping down .
perhaps also the most evident demonstration of the validity of my words is what we see today of the slowdown in implementing the demands of the revolution . besides , the desperate attempts to circumvent , steal , waste and revoke the revolution .
all this is due to the people 's revolt calming down . there has become no power sufficient to deter and eliminate the remnants of the previous regime .
