thousands of demonstrators gathered on friday and called it the friday of " purification " or " revolution first " or the " friday of retribution . " no matter how different the designations were , there was one goal , friday was a revolution against the military council " the council of deficiencies . "
the demonstration was against the transitional stage which is ruled by the military council . . i wish that i could hear the whole square shouting , saying " the people demand the removal of the marshal . " it was wonderful that all classes of people and especially the political parties gathered , despite the altercations between the youth of the revolution and the muslim brotherhood at the beginning , but the cry of the muslim brotherhood
" all of us together are one hand " calmed people down . . since all were there for one goal .
first . . judging the officers fairly who were behind the killing of martyrs , especially after they were declared innocent by the court , but the endeavors of " essam sharaf " will not succeed in calming down the demonstrators . therefore , he issued a decision to sack these officers , but the order has not been yet carried out by the ministry of interior , because it objected to their dismissal after they were declared innocent ! !
second . . trying mubarak and al-adli in a public court , of course , this is one of the simplest rights of the egyptian people especially for the families of the martyrs who have a fire inside of them that has not yet been abated .
third . . purging the government of some ministers " from the remnants of the former regime " and frankly i do not know why the military council is sticking to them ! ! unless they were fans .
and finally . . the demonstrators ' decided to hold a sit-in in the square until saturday until their demands are met , but in vain , and essam sharaf 's statement was not issued until yesterday " and no one knew the reason for the delay " , but essam sharaf 's speech was extremely frustrating , so the demonstrators decided to call for a new one-million-man march next tuesday .
note . . to the respected sirs who are against the trial of mubarak and those who say that the revolution is destroying egypt : with my respect , they don 't understand anything .
in principle , the one whose hand is in water is not like the one whose hand is in fire . i mean that no one will feel the fire of the families of martyrs except the families of martyrs and the one who has a martyr whose youth was trampled under the feet of the corrupt , and god willing , their blood will not go uncompensated , even if all egyptians are be martyred . . and the great egyptian people , the people of dignity , do not deserve to live except with dignity and honor .
