what is the reason that the fuel pump is broken ?
is it the delay in changing the fuel filter ?
is it because of the impurities in the 80 octane fuel ?
is it delaying refilling until only 10 liters are left in the tank ?
the oil pump is broken because of the negligence in cleaning the filter
and therefore the impurities gather in the filter
and after the filter is full of impurities , it is not able to do its job as a cleaner of the fuel impurities .
so it leaks into the pump and causes a blockage in it .
so the pump is forced to increase its effort to be able to deliver the fuel to the injection unit in the motor
at the end there is one result for all that you have written
80 octane fuel means a lot of impurities
if you leave the tank empty with low-quality fuel in the car like 80 octane this means a lot of impurities in the tank
and you will find the pump sucking up the fuel and the impurities .
by the way , the impurities have nothing at all to do with the type of fuel
because the problem is in the cleanliness of the gas pump in the station where you fuel up
because you can put 92 octane and it goes through the filter full of impurities and this is tested
certainly 80 octane is connected with low quality stations
certainly 80 octane is connected with not number one stations
so it is normal that it isn 't clean , especially as the majority of big stations stopped buying it
so it is normal that it isn 't clean , especially as the majority of big stations stopped bringing it
try to change the filter after each 100 km as this is better
i have not completed 100 km , only nearly 300 km in 5 months ! and the pump is broken , praise to allah
i don 't know , but maybe the fuel tank needs cleaning because the car was made in 1997 ?
i don 't know , but maybe the fuel tank needs cleaning because the car since 1997 ?
but i do not know whether this matter costs a lot or not !
peace be upon you . . there is another important thing which is the pump you have , like new cars , is powered by electricity
and can remain functioning for hours during travelling
and of course it warms up and it is designed to depend upon a high-fuel level in the tank to cool it down
which means that less than a quarter of the tank warms the pump up-
and it can burn out + there is more chance of the impurities entering the fuel circulation when the tank is almost empty
and this blocks the pump filter , this is not the main filter , and increases the suction load on the pump
so to summarize , you should fill up at a reputable station and do not forget the minimum limit for the tank
