after the court issued its ruling acquitting all the officers involved in the cases of killing the demonstrators , since the case had been referred to the criminal court
the court said that , after reviewing the penal code ,
it decided that all the officers accused in the case were found innocent ,
while referring the civil lawsuit to the specialized court
immediately upon announcing the verdict , the court turned into a place for wailing and crying by the families of the martyrs ,
with the mothers and wives of the martyrs shouting , " oh , my sons . . oh , my sons . . we will take the rights of our sons by our own hands ! "
on his part , wael suleiman - the lawyer for the families of the martyrs - said
that the verdict was unjust and that he had provided to the court proof of the defendants ' involvement through cell phone cards and cds containing scenes showing the officers as they opened fired on the demonstrators
he added that perhaps if the court had based its belief on the inquiries of the detective department , the police would never indict themselves
besides this , security forces have imposed a strict security cordon around the courthouse since early morning ,
this and security forces have imposed a strict security cordon around the courthouse since early morning ,
a thousand congratulations
all search procedures and operations have been tightened ,
and the families of the martyrs were prevented from entering the courtroom
also the defendants did not appear inside the dock during the pronouncement of the verdict
in the initial reasons that it laid out for the innocence of the defendants , the court said
that it had been established through investigations that the first and second defendants , captain shadi mohammed abdul hamid and captain ihab abdel-monem al-saeedi , had opened fire on the demonstrators
however , they had been in a situation of self-defense ,
because the demonstrators had been attacking the police station and trying to set it on fire ,
and in this case , the law grants the defendants the right to self-defense and to fire bullets at the demonstrators .
regarding the other three defendants , they provided the court with proof that they had not been present at the station during the incidents ,
while the court said that the victims in the lawsuit had tried to set the department on fire and attack it .
a thousand , thousand congratulations
it indicated that it firmly believes in the innocence of the defendants ,
and that it will lay out the reasons for the verdict in detail within thirty days of its pronouncement .
