the first thing i would like to talk about is what it means to be a veiled girl .
the veiled girl is the girl who wears her clothing according to the islamic characteristics of wearing the veil , which most of us know well and which includes : ( ( that it must not be tight , namely be loose , not-descript , not see-through , and not be an adornment in and of itself - - nor clothing for fame and display .
and that the girl should be free from the things that invalidate the veil uniform , such as perfume and high heels .
therefore , not every girl who is wearing a scarf can be said to be veiled .
the second thing i would like to say is that the veil is as obligatory as prayer . well , as we all pray , do we pray properly ? in other words , is the prayer of every one of us acceptable ? is every one of us submissive in his prayer ?
this means that everything is relative .
the third point i see is that the niqab and the veil are not a symbol of respect and decency for any girl , but finery cloth , on the other hand , is merely an act of disobedience and a challenge to allah !
lastly , i ask allah to help us all to wear a lawful veil that causes him to be pleased with us and grant us pleasant death , and that everyone should act according to his or her clothing and not treat anyone poorly .
peace be upon you
guys , this question recurs frequently in my mind , and i would like you to join me in thinking about it .
and the question is very conspicuous : is every girl wearing the hijab respectable ?
i will begin the answer .
i believe that all veiled girls - - of course i mean some but not all of them - - are not necessarily respectable , and likewise , not every girl who is not wearing the veil is not respectable . on the contrary , i see unveiled girls who are very respectful and veiled girls to whom the veil means nothing , and god only knows why they wear the veil ! maybe they wear it as a sort of fashion statement , for example . i would like to hear your opinion .
hi , asert al-ahzaan .
it 's not a lesson , of course !
there is a difference between a girl who wears the veil willingly out of conviction , aware of all of the dimensions to wearing it , and regarding it as a part of her overall behavior , and a girl who wears it because it was imposed on her because all those around her are veiled , and because she regards it as a custom and fails to respect it .
there is a difference between someone who behaves in any situation based on a particular principle on which he is convinced , and another one who only behaves to satisfy people !
man is not supposed to judge others only by appearance . there are other factors that influence the process of evaluating any girl you see .
peace to you , my sentimental sister . your question is beautiful ( is every girl wearing the veil respectable ? )
i would like to tell you that i support the opinion of our beautiful friend that there are some girls upon whom the veil may be imposed , but this is not a measure of course ; and there are some girls , like me , praise be to allah , who wear the veil on their conviction and faith that such an act brings them closer to allah , and because it is necessary for their decency .
but i would like to add that any respectable girl in general , whether she is wearing veil or not , is known through her behavior . wearing the niqab and not only the veil does not mean leaving home without parental permission or not respecting the opinion of one 's elders , or knowing many young people and going out with them , and then , at the end of the day , say that this is the current mode today .
or to be engaged and then appear to people or in front my partner or myself with an improper appearance and behave in a way that degrades me . this is not acceptable , of course .
there are many non-veiled girls , however , and their clothing is decent and their actions are polite . and the issue of conviction and faith to these girls regarding the veil comes over time . and thank you for such a nice subject .
this is not the norm .
the veil may be formal or a kind of cloth behind which a girl conceals many things .
hi everybody . i believe that any veiled girl must be decent because she is viewed as an interface to religion .
is every girl wearing the veil respectable ?
i knew the traffic authority would apply the idea of new license plates that included numbers and characters . this is of course because there are many vehicles , and the issue of such numbers has become of no avail .
but i thought what would happen , in view of the fact that some people select the numbers they like and others take what they accidently find , as well as the fact that plate numbers in egypt explicitly reflect the social status and importance of the owner of the car . i mean , no one in egypt can obtain a 4 -digit license plate . of course this is not a matter of divine action . no . it 's a very big business and there is bribe money to be paid in such matters .
but if , for example , you found a license plate such as : l . w . h 654 , it is impossible , of course , for me to accept such a plate , much less the kids in the streets who could barely read it as they kept laughing at me coming and going and saying , " the lwh ( signifying an indifferent man ) has come , the lwh has gone . " it 's something bad , isn 't it ?
the same applies for plates with symbols g . h . sh ( refers to a donkey ) , z . f . t ( signifying a bad man ) , b . a . f ( signifying an idiot ) , and b . gh . l ( signifying a mule ) . however , famous mule shopkeepers in al-mahala and mansoura will seek such a symbol to buy at any price because they find it very appealing .
of course there will be high-priced numbers such as h . l . w ( beautiful ) , q . m . r ( beautiful like a moon ) , and a . s . l ( as sweet as honey ) , but such plates will be confined to the sons of top officials and the country 's vips .
all i hope is that our talk about traffic predicts well and that i don 't face problems when i go to the authorities to get my plate . i 'm a man who sits on the fence ; neither wants to be l . w . h , nor a . s . l . it 's sufficient to me to be l . s . a . do you agree with me or what ?
i don 't believe in the numbering system in egypt . frankly , the plates i have written are very embarrassing .
