he was a physics student - - imagine !
thanks a lot basim for your presence and participation . your presence just makes us happy .
the student said , " we can drop the barometer from the top of the skyscraper and measure how much time it takes to reach the ground , and then we can calculate the skyscraper 's height using the law of gravity .
if the sun is shining , we can measure the length of the barometer , the length of the skyscraper 's shade , and of the barometer 's shade ; then we know the skyscraper 's height from the law of proportionality between the lengths of the two shadows .
if we want a quick solution that eases our minds , the best way to measure the skyscraper 's height using the barometer is to say to the skyscraper 's guard , ' i 'll give you this new barometer as a gift if you tell me how high this skyscraper is . '
if we want to complicate matters , we can calculate the height of the skyscraper by calculating the difference between the atmospheric pressure on the surface of the earth and on top of the skyscraper using a barometer . "
the expert waited for the fourth answer to demonstrate the student 's understanding of physics , while the student believed that the fourth answer was the worst because it was the most difficult and complicated .
that student was " niels bohr , " who not only succeeded in physics , but was the only danish person to win the nobel prize in physics . it 's life !
in the physics exam at the university of copenhagen , denmark ,
one of the exam questions was as follows : how do you define how high a skyscraper is using a barometer ( air pressure measuring device ) ?
the correct answer is the measurement of the difference between the atmospheric pressure on the surface of the ground and on the roof of the skyscraper .
one of the answers provoked the physics professor and made him decide to fail the student without reading the rest of his answers to other questions .
the provocative answer was : tie the barometer to a long rope and drop it from the top of the skyscraper until the barometer touches the ground - - then i measure the length of the rope .
the professor was angry because the student measured the height of his skyscraper in a primitive way that had nothing to do with the barometer or physics . however , the student complained , asserting that his answer was 100 % correct , and according to the rules of the university , an expert was appointed to decide on the case .
the expert 's report stated that the student 's answer was correct , but that it didn 't indicate a knowledge of physics , and it was decided that the student was to be given another chance to prove his scientific knowledge .
he was then asked the same question by the expert orally .
the student thought a little and said , " i have many answers , but i don 't know which one to choose . " the expert said , " say everything you have . "
