prevention is represented in the following points :
personal hygiene by washing hands well , avoiding rubbing the eyes and nose with an unclean hand as the first line of defense , as well refraining from eating any uncooked vegetables and fruit before making sure they are well washed .
bird breeders should lock birds in cages to prevent wild birds and migratory birds from mixing with them .
breeders of birds in closed poultry farms should get rid of workers who breed household birds by having them choose between leaving work or getting rid of their birds , in addition to affixing wires on the windows and covering feed to prevent birds from reaching them so as not to infect farm poultry .
refraining from hunting or approaching migratory birds and resident birds in anticipation of the possibility of transmission of the virus from other migratory birds , and particularly water fowl .
in hungary , hungary 's government said that the united states , britain and russia expressed their interest in the vaccine trial in hungary to fight the deadly bird flu virus after initial tests on humans proved to be promising .
we will have to start over with the process of vaccine development carried out by the national center for epidemiology in collaboration with omni invest if there is another strain other than h 5 n 1 that infects humans .
the french company ( sanofi - aventis ) developed an anti-h 5 n 1 strain vaccine , which was effective in creating an immune response among adults who enjoy good health .
the u . s . government ordered two million doses of the vaccine produced by sanofi for storage and is negotiating with the company to order more doses .
one of the birds being examined
the bird flu virus , scientifically called h 5 n 1 - - one of the types of viruses that infects birds
it 's a very dangerous virus if transmitted directly to humans , because it does not spread to humans from the air , but rather the infected person would be in an environment with infected birds , which would lead to contacting them in any manner and cause the transmission of infection from birds to humans .
cooked birds do not cause infection if they are eaten , but infection is transmitted to humans through the mucus of the infected bird 's nose , eyes or feathers .
amid this concern , the bird hunting committee in a shooting club thought of contributing to this issue with the expertise of its members .
currently , there 's a map of arrival sites for migratory birds as well as dates of arrival and flight from resting places - - in addition to the places where the birds stay for the duration of their migration .
the committee has already prepared a summary report on the virus , which stated , " this deadly virus infects birds in principle and was not transmitted to humans . however , in 2003 , 150 cases of human infection were detected , of which 60 died , mostly from among children and the elderly who suffered from respiratory problems .
the virus is transmitted from an infected bird to humans through the secretions of the nose , mouth and waste matter , as well as through secretions of the feather glands in the feathers and skin , in addition to the lachrymal secretions of the eye . in its current form , it constitutes a danger to life , but it is not a pandemic , as only one case of transmission from one person to another has been recorded .
most indicators suggest that when this virus encounters the normal influenza virus , it will be able to mutate and spread between humans directly , which makes it a destructive epidemic that is expected to kill millions of people .
