el-baradei became very famous when he highlighted the absence of weapons of mass destruction in iraq , which was the pretext given by the united states to invade iraq in 2003 .
ole danbolt , chairman of the nobel board , stated that awarding the prize to el-baradei and the iaea did not imply any criticism of washington , which differed with el-baradei concerning iraq .
he stated during a press conference : " this is not a kick in the leg to any state . "
the value of the prize , named after swedish scientist alfred nobel , amounted to 1 . 3 million dollars .
it is scheduled to be delivered in the norwegian capital of oslo on december 10 .
the nobel peace prize for 2004 went to wangari maathai , a kenyan advocate of environmental protection .
dr . mohamed el-baradei is awarded the nobel peace prize and the international atomic energy agency ( iaea ) is proud of him .
the board supervising the nobel peace prize in oslo said on friday that the atomic energy agency and its director general , egyptian scientist dr . mohamed el-baradei , were awarded the nobel peace prize .
the board added on its website that it had awarded the prize to el-baradei and the iaea in recognition of their efforts to reduce the spread of atomic weapons .
the board also praised el-baradei and described him as a courageous advocate of measures that enhance efforts to reduce the spread of weapons .
it declared : " the iaea 's role acquires great importance at a time when disarmament efforts appear to have reached a deadlock - - at a time when fears of the spread of nuclear weapons to states and terrorist groups arose , and at a time when nuclear powers are again playing a significant role . "
in the first reaction to the award , a spokeswoman for the agency stated at a press conference that the international atomic energy agency was " very proud of its director general , mohamed el-baradei . "
el-baradei has been the director of the international atomic energy agency ( iaea ) since 1997 . during his years of work , he supervised un efforts to search for secret nuclear weapons programs in iraq , iran , libya and north korea .
the norwegian nobel board chose the iaea and el-baradei from among a large number of candidates that totaled 199 individuals .
el-baradei and the iaea were among the potential candidates for the prize , whose timing coincided with the 60 th anniversary of atomic bombs being dropped on the two japanese cities of hiroshima and nagasaki in august , 1945 .
