a ten-year-old boy studies mathematics at the university
amir abu fariha is a ten-year-old boy form negev , who was admitted to the open university to start his studies and obtain a ba in mathematics .
amir abu fariha is only ten years old , but he is an excellent student in the department of mathematical sciences at the open university in israel . in addition amir 's two sisters study with him in the same university : yasmine , a 14 -year-old girl , and rana a 13 -year-old girl .
their mother works as a an english teacher in tel sheva , and their father is a road engineer .
all the children in abu fariha 's family are prominent in negev , but amir was promoted from third grade in the primary to the fifth grade , as a result of his extraordinary excellence in mathematics which made him feel constantly bored during his lessons .
initially , amir 's sisters were enrolled in the open university in a ba ( program ) in mathematics , so the father inquired whether his son , who was still in primary school , could also enroll .
at that point , they accepted him and he started studying for a ba in mathematical sciences .
how unfortunate , because he is israeli .
