the figures indicate that there is one egyptian man who from the area of imbaba named hossam abdul-baki who converted to judaism in israel and worked as a tourism agent . he adopted the name haim after he married a jewish girl , and , accordingly , his egyptian nationality was dropped , and when he tried to restore his egyptian nationality , the egyptian authorities refused his request .
with the increasing talk about egyptian-israeli marriages , dr . nasr farid wasel , former grand mufti of egypt , issued a fatwa stating that marriage to a woman who holds israeli nationality is legally forbidden , even if she is a christian or muslim arab .
most often , egyptian men , not girls , marry someone from the state of the enemy , despite the fact that both christianity and islam prohibit marriage to a jewish girl .
el-sharq el-awasat , el-wafd and al-bayan stated :
there are 17 thousand egyptians who work in israel according to the official statistics of 200 .
there is no problem with one who goes to israel for tourism or to visit , but in one who sells himself and his country intentionally or unintentionally to israel , which will seize the opportunity to penetrate egyptian society and recruit some youth to spy on their country after yielding to the temptations of money , sex and other things .
the reality confirms the absence of any accurate statistics about the number of egyptians working in israel , because there are many conflicting figures . for example , dr . amina al-jundi , minister of social affairs , issued an official statement in 200 indicating that the number of egyptians working in israel was 17 thousand people , while other sources stated that there were only 200 people .
at the same time , the official statements on statistics included in the israeli yearbook confirmed that the number of egyptians who entered israel as tourists in 200 amounted to 12 , 500 people , most of whom left after the end of the period of stay specified for them .
a few days ago the israeli central bureau of statistics announced in its annual report that foreign workers in israel who hold work permits were brought from 100 countries , such as thailand , whose workers represent 28 % of total workers , followed by the philippines , whose workers represent 20 % , then china at 10 % . concerning illegal employment in israel , it represents up to 23 % of the volume of employment , with 13 % of workers coming from jordan and 10 % from egypt , brazil and mexico .
the report explained that egyptians comprised 13 % of the employment total of muslims working in the israeli army , followed by jordanians and palestinians .
a scandal was triggered by member of parliament saber abul-futouh in his parliamentary question addressed to dr . ahmed nazif , prime minister , about the egyptian labor force in israel . the mp confirmed in his question that 13 % of the volume of egyptian labor in israel , estimated at around 17 thousand people , work in the israeli army .
the report also pointed out that the israeli army depended on egyptian labor because they obeyed orders , and they received 20 dollars per day in addition to two free meals . most egyptians in israel live in the areas of beersheba and haifa , and a small percentage in tel aviv .
17 thousand egyptians serving in the israeli army !
what is the cause of this catastrophe ?
do hunger , poverty , corruption and striving to earn a living make us serve in the army of our enemy ?
when i pondered the matter , i found that every house had a martyr , an injured person , or even a person who fought in the october ' 73 war . so why do we humiliate ourselves to this extent by accepting that our children go to serve in the army of our enemy ?
now the question is : how could it be that egyptians serve in the israeli army ? and regardless of the nature of their work in the army of the enemy , to whom will they be loyal in the event of a war ?
the al-hayat newspaper stated in a report that there are thousands of cases of marriage between egyptian men and israeli women according to the latest israeli census on the number of egyptian-hebrew marriages .
among these cases , there are 13 cases of marriages involving jewish women , while the rest of the wives belong to israeli arabs , most of whom belong to the azazma tribe . at a time when government agencies maintains the invalidity of these figures , the reality confirms the growing infiltration of egyptians to israel via jordan .
hence , the increasing number of cases of marriage to israeli women , the result of which are children who hold both egyptian and israeli nationality .
the report , issued last week by the israeli central bureau of statistics , explained that the number of young egyptian men married to israeli women amounted to 10 thousand young people , distributed among the cities of beersheba , haifa and tel aviv .
statistics confirm that most of these marriages involve daughters of israeli arabs , while the number of egyptians who married jewish women does not exceed 13 young men , especially after the israeli citizenship law imposed many restrictions on the marriage of egyptian men to israeli women .
meanwhile , the egyptian government tries to refute these numbers , claiming they are exaggerated .
in 2001 , the egyptian ministry of justice announced that the number of cases of marriag between egyptian and jewish women did not exceed 120 cases , registered in official documents , including 50 cases of egyptian girls married to young israeli arabs . these young people belong to the azazma tribe , a bedouin tribe in which half of its people belonging to egypt while the other half belong to israel . the majority of these young people are relatives regardless of their nationality .
