the egyptian constitution articles that should be amended
b - the party should get at least 3 % of the total elected people 's assembly and shura council 's members or the equivalent percentage in either council .
c - the party candidate should be one of the members of the supreme body of the party , with a term of one year completed in the supreme authority
3 - oversight of elections :
that awkward article stipulates that a special committee called , " the presidential election committee " shall be in charge of elections oversight , and its chairman shall be the president of the supreme constitutional court . .
how can that be ? the president of the supreme constitutional court is appointed by the president of the republic !
4 - nomination of independent candidates :
article 76 ignored the right of independent people to be nominated .
it does not indicate this right in any of its paragraphs , which is an inherent right under article 75 of the same constitution , and which states :
" the nominee for the office of president of the republic must be born in egypt and to egyptian parents ,
and have civil and political rights ,
why should these articles be amended ?
and should be no less than forty years old . "
article 75 does not stipulate that the candidate belong to any party .
it stipulates that he must be born in egypt to egyptian parents , and have civil and political rights . .
maybe it considers every independent candidate not an egyptian !
- -
article 77 : see the constitution to read the full article .
why should it be amended ?
this article stipulates that the term of the presidency is for six gregorian years ;
this is a long term in comparison to most constitutions of other countries in the world . .
that same article stipulates the re-election of the president for additional terms , without specifying the number of such terms ,
article 76 on electing the president ; this article has a number of blunt errors and unfair conditions which impede any fair elections .
which supports the continuation of a dictatorial regime which rules the country by fraudelent elections , which is happening at the present time .
- -
see the constitution to read the full article .
this article basically aims to exclude the judiciary from overseeing the electoral process by consituting a higher committee which has nothing to do with the process of overseeing elections ;
and which can be very easily controlled by the ruling regime .
thus , the electoral process will be a farce whose results are known beforehand .
dear brother , egyptian citizen ! we should unite our efforts in order to amend the constitution /
if you don 't participate today , don 't complain tomorrow !
the most important are :
1 - accepting the nomination for the presidency :
accepting a nomination for the presidency has unusual and illogical terms , such as the condition of support from an exaggerated number of members of the people 's assembly , shura council , and local councils .
2 - parties ' participation in the electoral process :
accepting a nomination is also associated with a number of unfair terms for the political parties , and a blatant interference in their affairs .
this article has the following condition for accepting the party candidate :
a - a lapse of five consecutive years at minimum from the date of the party 's foundation , with uninterrupted practice of their activities during that period .
article 1 , means that the candidate should be mohamed , gamal , mohamed , gamal , mohamed , gamal , or mohamed .
article 2 , that the presidencial term shouldn 't be less than 35 , 50 or may be 100 years .
and the last article emphasizes the importance of dictatorship , rather democracy .
indeed , all these articles must be amended .
