2 . enabling the egyptian judiciary to completely supervise the electoral process as a whole
3 . controlling the elections via civil society organizations , at local and international levels .
4 . providing equal opportunities in the media for all candidates , especially in presidential elections .
5 . enabling the egyptians abroad to exercise their right to vote at embassies and consulates .
6 . ensuring the right to run for presidential elections without arbitrary restrictions in line with egypt 's obligations under the international convention on civil and political rights , and limiting the right to run for the presidential elections to two terms .
7 . participating in the elections by using the national id number . the achievement of some of those procedures and safeguards requires amending articles 76 , 77 and 88 of the constitution as soon as possible .
i would like to emphasize in this regard that the national association of change opens it door to all egyptians inside and outside egypt who agree with the need to change , starting with the achievement of said safeguards and procedures with respect to the elections , and concluding with a new constitution that guarantees every egyptian the right to free and dignified life and marks the beginning of a comprehensive social and economic reform program , so that the people will be the ruler in the end .
the foremost objective of the association is not limited to changing the rules on running for presidential elections , but rather the pursuit of comprehensive change by mobilizing public support for this purpose in a peaceful manner .
