in the light of my meetings with all the various egyptian political and religious affiliations , including men and women , from among the representatives of civil society and young people , i found out that there was unanimous agreement on the need for change in egypt .
for this reason , there was general agreement on the need to unite all the voices calling for change within the national association of change , which i was asked to lead and support , as a general framework under which all the voices calling for change are united .
the main objective of the association is to work toward establishing a political system based on true democracy and social justice ,
the first step on this path is to ensure the basic guarantees of free and fair elections , for all egyptians , so that there is an equal opportunity for all , whether it be in legislative or presidential elections .
these are guarantees and procedures demanded by broad groups of egyptian society for many years , particularly : 1 . ending the emergency state
