the matter became confusing . . which of them was being prepared to succeed his father ?
was it the gloomy and sullen one ?
or the dancing and smiling one ?
no one say to me that they are away from the scene and that what is happening is a natural thing ,
because changing article 76 in the constitution was neither pointless nor the result of looking for an absent democracy or free elections ,
{ { the political scene . . elbaradei has arrived , men } }
the article was specially changed to give an opportunity to one of them to nominate himself , on the basis that nomination for the presidency has become available to every egyptian citizen on certain conditions ,
it was a good coincidence that these conditions were not met except by one of them . the most prominent condition was to obtain a certain percentage of nomination from the members of the people 's assembly , the shura council , and the municipal councils , which the democratic national { sadness } dominates ,
which means that it 'll all stay within the family , man ,
which means that the operation is in its house , man ,
the more the time for next presidential elections approaches , the more the predictions , and the more hopes and dreams are revived that change might be on the way .
the more the decisive hour becomes near , images , events , and individuals appear on the political scene
allow me to describe the political scene as i see it now and from my modest point of view , which i have formed on the basis of monitoring the incidents and events that have recently taken place on the political scene
three figures have recently appeared on the political scene , each of whom is a candidate to succeed current president muhammad hosni mubarak - this , of course , in the event that mubarak leaves power by his own will -
even if the nature and the role of each of these three figures differs from the other , they remain the most prominent on the scene until this moment . maybe there will be more figures who will play a role in the next anticipated play , { let us vote } , which the ruling party writes and directs
the first character is the character of the egyptian citizen " gamal mubarak " - as they call him in mass media - the president 's younger son , who was the subject of predictions , conclusions , and analyses during the last five years , and who was and still is the major candidate to succeed his father whether we like or not ,
this character began to be groomed politically a long time ago , and to be pushed into the political and media life so that people become accustomed to seeing him . thus , he became a familiar face on the political scene , internally and externally ,
despite all of the criticism aimed at him , and despite the fact that he was not accepted by the general public , he remains the most favored candidate in the arena
others were not heard of except at that time , including names that had no political or partisan role on the basis that their parties were only known to a very few people
the basis on which i formed my opinion is the information resulting from the political situation and the planning of the regime to choose the next president
elbaradei is not a member of any of the wall-flower parties
and he does not have a party to support him
aside from this , if the regime felt any danger from his side , it would not allow him to become so prominent on the scene , even if he was protected by his former international capacity
but in the end , elbaradei remains one of the candidate characters to contest the next presidential elections
so who will eat the cake ?
and who will wash the dishes ?
as for the third character , which is expected to play the { supporting } role in this expected political scene , he is dr . " mohamed elbaradei "
that internationally-famous character
the former director of the united nation organization 's atomic energy agency , and the winner of the nobel peace prize
despite my full respect for the person of elbaradei and his international status , and despite my respect for every opinion that is counter to my opinion regarding the { supporting } role that i think that he will play either willingly or by being pushed to play it , this international character has recently come to the surface after he finished his international work , and after he declared that he was ready to nominate himself for the next presidential elections , and after he had been publicly received at the airport when he came home
despite all the nominations and support that he recently gained after his declaration from citizens who dream of change and of new blood to run through the veins of the state after bad blood continued to run through its veins during the last decades
also despite the criticism made of him , whether such criticism was objective or was meant to distort him politically and in the media on the basis that he did not participate in any of the political or social battles in egypt because he spent most of his life out of egypt and then fell on the egyptian land by means of a parachute , thinking that people are waiting for him with embraces to be the next president of egypt
and despite the second citizenship that he holds
i say that , despite all of this , what i have understood today from elbaradei 's talk on dream channel in al ashira masa 'an talk shaow , made me think that he will perform the support role that he performed in the past . in the last elections there were many characters , up to ten characters
