how then could this man squander a crumb of the bread that he had acquired with great effort and desperate struggle , so that the heart of this poor man reached in its cruelty that he would say to himself , let the mouse go to hell , the important thing is that i and my children would feel full
but the mouse died of hunger and he and his children were not full .
perhaps some might wonder , why don 't the mice get together and decide to migrate to high class areas and live the homes of the rich so that they would find enough food to appease their hunger and the hunger of their children
the answer here comes from ( farfour al-khanshour ) the head mouse of boulaq aboul ela neighborhood , so what did it say ?
once upon a time , after things became difficult for us here in boulaq aboul ela neighborhood , and after the poverty of the poor increased and the inhabitants of the homes we lived in no longer found what appeases their hunger let alone leave us crumbs to feed on - some young mice decided to take the risk and cross to the other bank of the nile to reach the posh zamalek neighborhood .
because they were certain that this posh neighborhood whose inhabitants live in luxury is where they will find a livelihood of abundance .
indeed a large group of them congregated at the bank of the nile on the side of boulaq aboul ela and decided to wait till the great river granted them a floating tree trunk or a piece of wood that had lost its way from a poor fishing boat -
and after waiting for several weeks , in which some died of hunger , the river bestowed on them a small piece of wood , so they decided to get on it and attempt to row to reach the other side of the river
indeed they crowded around it , each wanting to have precedence , and as the piece of wood was small it was not wide enough to accommodate this large crowd of migrating mice so many died from the severe overcrowding and some fell in the river and was swallowed by the water
when the piece of wood moved across the river , buffeted by the currents of water and toyed with by the tide , in the end less than half the mice that got on the piece of wood reached the other side , while the others drowned or died of severe hunger .
in the old days they used to say about a very poor man that if the mouse ever entertained the thought of living in the house of that poor man he will die of hunger because he will not find any scraps of this poor man 's food to feed on or even furnishings to nibble
anyway , those of them who made it to the other side were fatigued , very tired and deadly hungry , but they fought their fatigue consoling themselves with plenty of food and a plentiful livelihood , and each went to find itself a house to live in
the last part of this incident is told by a mouse with only three legs , that is the only one who returned from this deadly trip after he lost his fourth leg in the mouth of a vicious cat . it says
when we went off to find homes to live in , we were surprised , and as if the doors of hell were opened to us , from pretty looking cats - wearing red bows around their necks and sometimes golden chains and seemed not to have tasted the flesh of mice before as they are used to beef , corned beef and hot dog - so they decided to taste the mice meat that it had heard of in grandmother 's tales around the fireplace in the cold months of winter , so the battle was heated and outcome was known ;
in addition to electric traps , ordinary traps , sticky materials , poisonous materials , not to mention the traditional weapons such as brooms and plastic flip flops that have a flower on them
and those who escaped this heated battle were either run over by the cars in the street , stepped on by the feet of pedestrians , or picked out by homeless cats , and the only thing that saved me from this hell was leaving my leg in the mouth of a vicious cat and returning home afloat on a watermelon rind
