student rana abou bakr who graduated top of high school in the republic in the " science " branch launched a vicious attack on the system , accusing it of being responsible for destroying the educational process and turning egypt from a country with a renowned position in the fifties and sixties of the last century to a country that comes at the tail end of the world as a result of the rising corruption in all fields , especially education .
rana , who is seventeen years old , indicated that the millions who go to schools do not benefit from the various education curricula , and the country does not take care of them , instead it contributes to destroying their future by not providing good opportunities for studying .
the top student revealed that her father was the one who pushed her to immigrate to the united states to seek knowledge and build a future and told her ( there is nothing here and it is not possible in any way to expect excellence , instead you might end up staying at home and joining the millions of unemployed ) .
she said that she decided to take her father 's advice and added that she hasn 't decided yet if she was going to return in the future to work in egypt in the field of medicine after she finishes her studies or if she will remain in america all her life , indicating that the advanced level of medical research there lures any student to leave egypt .
rana abou bakr attributed her desire to finish her studies in america to what she described as the ' poor ' educational system in egyptian universities now , which is not conductive of any accurate scientific research or be creative in practical study . this makes rana the first top high school graduate in the republic who decides not to finish her university studies in egypt , as confirmed by dr . seddik abdel salam , president of the ' top high school students ' association .
