travelers at the garage of pullman in lattakia city on the syrian coastline were surprised at the entry of a newspapers vendor aged around sixty carrying a number of the official al-wehda newspaper
and calling out among the passengers the news of the suicide of the egyptian president hosni mubarak
the amusing thing is that the vendor didn 't make any noteworthy effort , and within a few minutes of the people 's hearing the news he had sold out all the quantity he had at three times its price which is not more than three syrian lira ,
for this sale to become the fastest of its kind in the history of the local paper because it is one of the newspapers that is not read by many like the other local official papers .
the vendor disappeared very quickly after leaving everyone turning the pages of the newspaper to no avail in search of the mentioned news till they discovered that they were victims of a naughty prank done " that falls under fraud " by a newspaper vendor in order to sell all the papers he had ,
some swore at him and other laughed a lot at what happened , but the only consolation that remains is that the newspaper will be in their hands till they go home .
a qualitative shift in selling local newspapers ! !
