he received his primary education at victoria college in alexandria and the american school in mansoura ,
then received his preparatory education at mansoura preparatory school for boys ,
he was the president of the student union of the school and the governorate throughout the three years of preparatory education ,
he was elected as the ideal student in dakahleya governorate
he received his secondary education at al-malek al-kamel secondary school in mansoura , and was the president of the student union at the school , at the level of the administration and the governorate ,
he was elected at the president of the general student union for secondary and technical schools , and teachers schools and institutes throughout the secondary school stage .
nour graduated from the faculty of law , mansoura university ,
was the president of the student union for two years ,
has a diploma in international law ,
then got a masters in the philosophy of political history ,
before you answer the question , get to know dr . ayman nour
then he got a doctorate degree from the academy of higher sciences " arab world institute " history department with distinction . the topic of the dissertation was about " the islamic movement in egypt from 1980 to 1990 " .
early emergence
he went into journalism early on , working as an amateur journalist while studying , and then into professional journalism with the publication of the first issue of the al-wafd newspaper , the mouthpiece of the wafd party ,
he continued to promote at al-wafd till he became the editor in chief in 1984 ,
he continued to write a fixed column in it titled " diary of a riotous journalist " for more than 16 years ,
he writes several weekly articles in some national , independent and party newspapers , such as october magazine , al-ahrar newspaper , and al-maidan newspaper ,
he is one of the founders of al-horreya newspaper ,
he was a regional director for editing several arab and international newspapers such as al-hayat " london " , al-dawleya " paris " , al-madina " jeddah " , and al-fajr al-jadid " kuwait " , as well as working as a correspondent for the french radio in cairo .
he then went into party work , and was elected as the president of al-wafd youth committee in cairo , then general secretary of wafd in cairo , then secretary of the supreme wafd authority , then member in the supreme party authority ,
he then left the wafd party in march 2001 after the death of the wafd leader fouad serageddin following political differences with the new party leader dr . noaman gomaa amid a major political crisis to establish al-ghad party in october 2004 after it was rejected five times by the parties affairs committee .
his curriculum vitae
he went to parliamentary work , and was elected as a member in the people 's assembly ( parliament 's first chamber ) in the 1995 elections for bab el-she 'reya and el-moski directorate in central cairo , which is one of the busiest and most densely populated directorates in egypt , to become the youngest member of the egyptian parliament .
at the assembly , he was elected as the deputy of the opposition leader ,
in 199 , nour won the prize for best parliamentary performance for east mediterranean countries ,
he was re-elected as a parliament member in the following election in 200 for the same directorate .
wide activity
as for his relationship to social work , he was elected more than once as a member in the secretariat of the egyptian human rights organization , a member in the arab popular committee to support the intifada , based in damascus , and a president ( founder ) of nour benevolence society in central cairo from 1994 to present ,
he was also elected as member is several organizations interested in human rights and fighting corruption , and is the founder of the egyptian parliamentary committee to boycott israeli goods .
nour won the prize for best egyptian and arab parliamentary performance ,
he was elected as best parliamentary member in mediterranean countries , and received several local and international prizes in this field ,
his thirteen offices have received more than 27 thousand request and service , of which he achieved close to 95 % in some sectors .
his name is ayman abdel aziz nour , known as ayman nour ,
he led a campaign to beautify bab el-she 'reya square , where his electoral directorate lies ,
he built a statue for the son of bab el-she 'reya , the singer of generations mohamed abdel wahab with personal efforts ,
he played a big and tangible role in youth action through the activities of nour society ,
he organized tens of seminars , parties , and trips for youth for free ,
he also paid attention during his presence in the parliament to the problems of the people of his constituency of street vendors , and those who work in the shoes and leather industry in el-moski street ( the biggest commercial street in egypt ) , where he submitted more than one request for information to the government about them , and for which tens of laws were issued from 1995 to 2001 .
he submitted a draft for " arab parliament for young parliamentarians " , which was approved by the arab parliamentary union in its term in 2001 .
he got more than a third of the assembly 's votes when he applied for nomination for the post of assembly deputy in 200 , so he got 161 votes out of a total of 454 votes , to achieve a parliamentary precedence that never happened before .
nour wrote several books , the most famous of which is " political freedom in islam " , " liberalism is the solution " , " the black policeman zaki badr " , " diary of a riotous journalist " , " the gulf crisis , the assassination of kuwait " , and " who killed solaiman khater " .
