{ { this is the shrine of the authority on god , sheikh obama the american } }
so let 's review obama 's speech together and analyze it together according to the standards of american politics and not according to our dreams and delusions as arab nations .
so let 's follow obama 's speech together and analyze it together according to the standards of american politics and not according to our dreams and delusions as arab nations .
but before going into the details of the analysis , i must point out an important fact , which is the nature of politics in western countries in general and in america in particular .
because those politics are totally different than politics in the arab world and in the third world in general
our policies as arabs change with the change of whomever is in charge . if a president dies , and another president takes his place , the previous president 's policies will be crossed out and new policies drawn up that agree with the views of the new president with the stroke of a pen
this is what has made us fall backwards and never move forward , because we always start from the beginning .
this is what has made us fall backwards and never move forward , because we always start from the first line .
as for the west and in america , even though the president does not continue for more than two terms maximum , changes in the country 's public policies never occur . and even if some changes take place in internal policies from one president to another , there are always constants in the policies of those countries that do not change no matter how many presidents change and no matter the ruling party 's ideology
those policies remain ongoing and continuous . among them , for example , are the foreign policies related to the middle eastern countries , the islamic countries , and the eternal relationship between america and israel
of course in addition to the self-serving policies that form the majority of western policies in general .
so it is delusional to expect the change of those fixed policies with the change of a president , or even ten presidents
those policies are not governed by emotions or party ideology ; rather they are governed by the general interests of the state , which are determined by the constitution and the senate , and not the ruler .
i watched the speech of u . s . president obama , just like the majority of egyptian people and perhaps the majority of people
