here are their lies for you to judge them
1 - the lie of a united arab army
and the joint arab defense agreement
a dream of many of us that we jointly defend ourselves against external aggressions ,
this is stated by the united nations in its charter in article 51 that states , individually and collectively , have the right to defend themselves against external aggressions
a " treaty of joint defense and economic cooperation between the league of arab states " was already signed in 1950 , and all the member states of the league of arab states joined it
however , this treaty was never implemented even one time during the history of arabs
2 - united arab will
lies of the arab summit
we often tend to use the word " united " when we talk about the arab problems ,
this , of course , is permissible and acceptable , due to geographical and historical proximity ,
but the second row of leaders , including foreign ministers and official spokespersons and their aides , use this word in a crude and offensive way until this word became an old cliche that offends people more than it gives them enthusiasm
so , what does a united arab will mean ?
do the arab countries want to have a real will and thus want to meet and unite wills ?
are the arabs moved by their will or by the will of their leaders ?
are the leaders themselves moved by their own will or by the will of their personal interests and the instructions they receive from their seniors ?
all of these questions , whose answer is known in advance , expose this word to ridicule and mocking which is suitably applicable to the one who drawls this word
3 - arab common market
" since the league of arab states was established in 1945 , the idea of an arab common market has occupied the interest of the leaders of arab states " in the media only
meetings . . discussions . . disengagements , to no avail
meetings . . discussions . . disengagements , the guest is gone
every single summit discussed that idea and looked into ways to carry it out , thereby making further discussions about this market absolute nonsense
4 - the lie of a united arab currency
of course , as long as the idea of an arab common market was restricted by the leaders to forming joint arab committees , the idea of a united arab currency does not take steps beyond talks .
5 - the lie of the common stance
for every international , foreign-arab , or arab-arab problem , rulers and leaders call for the necessity of forming a united arab stance or compliance with the united arab position
in fact , there is nothing called " stance " nor is there something called " arab " , nor of course is there anything called " united " ,
each leader thinks that his personal stance should be the united arab position
6 - relations with iran
because iran is of a race that is different from the arab race which they strive to prove to be " singular " without having scientific evidence to prove that ; rather , on the contrary , all proofs indicate that arabs are of various races
and because iran has a language other than the arabic language ,
a message that i send to our arab rulers . .
and because iran has an ideology different from the group 's ideology " which has not been yet defined " ; based on these primary and other secondary principles , it appeals to many to consider iran " an enemy "
consequently , those who normalize with iran are among those who put themselves amidst us to cause devastation
in this way , iran is used , and it uses us , in a trite way , thus making talks about " the stance " toward iran something funny
7 - the lie of the arab nation being a single homeland
they say that the arab countries are one homeland and that we are one nation and that we are brothers
a single look at the airports of the arab states is sufficient to judge these empty pretentious sayings
it is sufficient to be an arab and to visit another arab country to realize that it is impossible to enter without a visa and that you need approval from security authorities here and there
and the strange thing is that an egyptian , for example , can enter malaysia without a visa , but he cannot enter qatar or kuwait without a visa
let us conciliate , because conciliation is good . let us conciliate
this is the slogan of any attempt to make conciliation between brothers
our rulers who have been addicted to the meeting table . .
the conciliation attempts start with a good initiative by one of the leaders to conciliate between two or more leaders
and the brothers sit together or absent themselves . in both cases , the result is the same
if they are absent , the outward and inward battles continue
if the brothers sit together , they share mutual feelings of love in appreciation of the brother who made the initiative , so that they would not let him down . and the brothers leave , each of them kissing the head of his brother , and everything is ok
if the brothers sit together , they share mutual feelings of love in appreciation of the brother who made the initiative , so that they would not let him down . and the brothers leave , each of them kissing the head of his brother , and milk is clear and cream is dairy
when the senior leaders return , major problems immediately surface once again
8 - the lie of the arab oil
( arabs use oil to boast over one another , and it effectively contributed only to fuel their internal wars )
since oil was discovered in the arab countries , we hear this word
the truth is that the discovery was not used to match the designation " arab oil " unless shortly before the october war , as it was not exported to the countries which helped israel . the countries that refused to export oil benefited from that , because they compensated the losses arising from withholding it by the difference of high prices , which was many times higher than before the oil was not exported
there are also people who say that many arab countries urged america and israel to wage war on egypt in 1967
our rulers who have been addicted to ending conflicts among themselves . .
since arab oil was used in this situation , the arab brothers do not stop reminding egypt of this favor
other than this , the word has been used for 35 years for local consumption
if oil should contribute to anything , then this thing is , of course , tension among the arab states to the extent of fighting and occupation as in the case of iraq and kuwait .
9 - the lie of arab national security
because the countries joining the league of arab sates extend from the ocean to the gulf , it is normal that they have neighboring states that pose a threat to their security ; therefore , the rulers surprise us with the importance of arab national security
consequently , the south of sudan poses a threat to arab national security
