the " sawasya " confirmed that what happened to the people of the town of al shuraniya , including setting fire to the houses of baha 'i citizens and forcing them out of their houses unjustly is counter to the law and charters of human rights in egypt and the world . it is also counter to the international covenant on human rights and to the principle that all people are equal in status and rights , and there must not be discrimination among them , and that they have full rights to freedom and personal security .
the center demanded , in a statement , the necessity that people deal with baha 'is as being part of egyptian society who have the same rights and duties , according to the constitution and in fulfillment of the principle of citizenship
in addition , everyone who lives on the land of egypt has the right to security , a fair trial , and sovereignty of law , regardless of his gender , religion , color , level of richness or poverty , or the social status of him or his family .
a statement issued by the center mentioned that families have the right to reside without restrictions being imposed on them because of race , gender , or religion . they also have the right to social security , fair employment conditions , and a degree of sufficient living . this is in addition to their rights to basic education regardless of their religion , gender , or financial abilities . they also have the right to health care
