the arrest warrants include cairo security director , ismaeil el-shaer , public security secret police director , adly fayed , central security forces head , ahmed ramzi , and state security director , hassan abdel-rahman .
the charges concentrate on their issuing of orders to open fire with live ammunition on the protesters on the twenty eighth of january / kanoun al-thani , which is known as " the day of wrath , "
and that they were responsible for those who fired .
if they are convicted of these charges , the four officers will face penalties ranging up to death .
it is noteworthy that the massive protests that were witnessed in the streets in cairo and the cities of egypt , which occurred on the twenty-fifth of january , and the clashes with the governmental security forces and some supporters who were known as thugs , resulted in the death of at least 384 deceased and more than six thousand injured .
the former egyptian interior minister , al-habib el-adly , was referred to the judiciary on saturday .
he is the first minister in mubarak 's regime to face prosecution .
he denied the charges against him which were similar to the charges against the four officials .
senior officers of the interior referred to the judiciary
while hundreds of egyptians gathered in tahrir square in the heart of cairo to participate in what was called the " march of millions " , the egyptian attorney general announced the detention of four senior interior ministry officials on charges that are considered serious .
the coalition of the youth of the revolution called for this demonstration under the title of " national unity " , in the wake of the sectarian clashes that have been recently witnessed in the country .
some armed forces officers in the square said to the bbc that protestors were allowed to stay in the square provided that they don 't go down to the street to avoid disrupting traffic .
the bbc reporter noticed this , as the gatherings were concentrated on the sides of the square which might not accommodate the protesters if the numbers continued to increase .
on the other hand , hundreds of copts held a sit-in in front of the egyptian tv building demanding the rebuilding of the church which was vandalized in the village of sool in the helwan governorate .
the number of participants in the sit-in is expected to increase after the copts called for a march of millions in front of the building .
senior officers .
the egyptian attorney general , abdel meguid mahmoud , decided to issue arrest warrants for 4 senior interior ministry officials and officers based upon the suspicion that they issued orders to shoot protestors during the demonstrations that demanded the overthrow of former president hosni mubarak 's regime .
