the aim as doctor fairuz says is to support and boost the role of the family in developing society on the basis that the family is the most important unit of civilian society .
for her part doctor inshad ezz el-din , lecturer in family social sciences , considers that the idea of this closed camp is doomed to failure as it is more akin to a school program that young people reject .
she went on to say that " this experiment delves into individual human feelings and tries to direct these feelings " .
she adds : " the way one person differs from another regarding how he thinks and behaves and his marital relationship makes it an issue that we need to prepare for because it is [ a lifetime relationship | the whole life that we will live . "
doctor inshad ezz el-din describes marital relations as an " arsenal " , and says : " it cannot take place through a set of scientific rules and training to apply them . " she considers that respect , maturity and understanding between husband and wife are the way forward , in addition to making some compromises on each side .
this in her view guarantees building an ideal marital relationship largely free of flaws .
masrawi asked a number of young people for their views on setting up a training camp before marriage .
there were those who supported and commended the idea while others strongly rejected it and felt it was not suitable to the egyptian society , while others found it ridiculous and called it a game .
there were those who supported and commended the idea while others strongly rejected it and felt it was not suitable to the egyptian society , while others found it ridiculous and thought that it looks like a game .
22 -year-old mohammed ibrahim al-sayyed supports the idea of the camp and says : " an activity such as this will help solve the problem of not being psychologically ready for marriage , the basic reason for most marital problems . "
to be honest the news bothered me a lot .
the law student goes on to say : " in addition to its providing an opportunity for more participation and interaction with family life and understanding it through the information and advice provided by the program so that the individual becomes ready to create a successful marital relationship . "
20 -year-old rami samir agrees with him , and as soon as he heard the idea said a common phrase used by many youth " peace man "
he said : " i have nothing against the experiment especially as it 's free and maybe it will be useful to those who experience it " , stating that the basic problem that the camp has to deal with is the boredom that afflicts married couples a short time after being married which is something that plagues every family .
ahmed awad , a bank employee , suggested that the idea should be fun and not complicated so that we convey the message that marriage is not a battle to be won by whoever imposes their personality on the other .
he said : " the camp is more like a game of " bride and groom " that we that we used to play long ago , as we used to share domestic chores with our close ones in an innocent playful way " .
he said : " the camp is more like a game of " bride and groom " that we that we used to play long ago , as we used to share domestic chores with our close ones in an innocent childlike way " .
on the other hand , 24 -year-old karim dhaifallah essentially rejects the idea asserting that the majority of those who would resort to it are failures who have achieved nothing in their lives and also girls who are not serious , as he described it .
daifallah , who works as a company accountant , said he would be embarrassed of taking part in a camp to prepare young people for marriage .
daifallah , who works as a company accountant , said he would be embarrassed of being a member of a camp to prepare young people for marriage .
his opinion is shared by first year science student amir tag who believes that the idea of the camp will offer nothing new .
the marital experiences an individual witnesses in daily life on the scope of relatives and through societal relations is sufficient to give him enough experience away from a complicated and boring educational approach .
as for 22 -year-old hiam saad , a social services institute graduate , she says that she would be shy to take part in a camp preparing young people for marriage , saying that she would be embarrassed about discussing this issue with her parents !
