the impact of the internet on public relations
so it became a fundamental source in the upbringing process . therefore it requires a key role by the family , school , and state in controlling the content of the internet to ensure control of the negative aspect , which may carry such content ,
professor of social psychology at the university of yarmouk , dr . adnan al-attoum explained the effect of the internet on social and psychological aspects ,
he said that the information and communications revolution as well as the spread of the internet in homes , institutions , and cafes , is considered a phenomenon that deserves attention and study to understand its social and psychological effects . it has also left its effects on many other aspects ,
and he said that the use of the internet by many people , especially segments of teenagers and youth , has become one of the phenomena that an ordinary person can see its reflections on everyone who interacts with these segments ,
the use of the internet has become a substitute for healthy social interaction with friends and relatives . the person of concern would start spending long hours exploring many web-sites , which means a change in the system of social values * * of individuals . whereas , this vast use , in turn , reinforces the individual values rather than the social and teamwork values , which represents an important component of our culture ,
he pointed out to the jordanian news agency that in return , the individual use of computers and the internet enhances the desire and inclination for loneliness and isolation amongst teenagers and young people , thus lessening the opportunities for interaction and healthy social and emotional growth , which is no less important for knowledge development , curiosity , and exploration ,
he said some preliminary studies suggest that the use of the internet exposes children and teenagers to imaginary and unrealistic material and information , thereby hindering their thinking and adaptation and it develops some irrational ideas , especially those related to personal relationships , lifestyle patterns , customs , and traditions prevailing in other communities ,
he added that the use of the internet has become a source of psychological , social , and economic stress for individuals , where the individual who doesn 't belong to the internet culture is exposed to the criticism from friends for not keeping up with the elements of this culture . this practice can be financially costly , especially for individuals who have no income .
dr . attoum explained that some of those concerned point to the fact that internet access to large areas of life has become a catalyst in strengthening the gap between generations with respect to computer culture and communication with the outside world ,
but many of those people who do not enjoy the advantage of using the internet have become exposed to the accusation of being backwards and stupid , which helps develop a pattern of social and cultural conflict between the generations , or segments of society , or between children and adults or children and parents ,
the impact of using the internet on social relations
as for the impact of internet use on the social and family life of young people , the jordanian news agency met with a number of young men and young women and samih al-mahdi akmil / 27 / years said , " i use the internet on a daily basis for at least two hours , " showing that the internet has an impact on our social relations . . " the time dedicated to my relationship with my family at home and with my friends diminished gradually and i spent the time instead on the computer . "
he said that the internet sometimes increases the social networking ,
for example , when the results of the high school grades came out , i received calls from a bunch of our relatives and friends who do not know how to use the internet to find out the results , and some of them came to the house in person . and the same thing with the results of the comprehensive exam , whereas many people who didn 't know how to use the internet , i find social networking with them by helping them with what they need .
mira farid ghattas , / 20 / years old , said , " i use the internet on an almost daily basis and i use it for about one to three hours " explaining that , " the internet has its positives , as it is better in economic terms , especially in the case of staying in touch and connecting with friends outside of the country . it also enhances relationships with people and friends outside the country and keeps us in continuous communication with them .
it also has its negatives . . a number of my friends use the computer about 7 hours a day . . and , i believe , that not all of this time has a definite benefit and thus negatively affects their social relationships . i consider that a waste of time and a waste of money as well as impacting negatively on their studies and their relationships with parents , "
fathi mazen gabriel said , " i use the computer every day for between four to five hours , and sometimes eleven hours straight . . and i think that the there are so many positive aspects to the internet . first , staying in touch and connecting with friends outside jordan . . my friends are scattered between the u . s . and canada and i 'm eager to communicate with them through the internet . "
he explained , " there is an important feature to the internet which is providing information on the spot . " he pointed out that he is interested in music and can find all of the information he needs on the internet . . " the internet also provides purchasing services so i can buy music cds that are not available in jordan through the internet . " thank you ,
