demanding an apology for the report and for it to be corrected to say that dr . zakaria azmi received 80 million telephone calls .
meanwhile , a professor of otolaryngology at ain shams university - who preferred to remain anonymous - asserted that the human body cannot handle this astronomical number of calls ,
and that talking continuously for a period of more than 12 hours causes adverse effects on the ear , throat , and vocal cords .
from a technical viewpoint , a telecommunications engineer said in a statement to " al- masry al-youm " that the period of 23 days that the president spent in germany only amounts to 33 , 00 minutes ,
a million calls on zakaria azmi 's telephone
and if we assume that dr . zakaria azmi spent all that time answering telephone calls with his mobile phone connected to the charger , then this scenario is absolutely impossible to materialize
because the smart chips and minute components of the phone set cannot withstand the overheating caused by this long period of talking , especially considering the charger connection which raises the battery temperature , leading to its damage and causing the mobile phone to stop working .
because the smart chips and minute components of the device cannot withstand the overheating caused by this long period of talking , especially considering the charger connection which raises the battery temperature , leading to its damage and causing the mobile phone to stop working .
he added that even if each call lasted only ten seconds , the time spent by dr . zakaria azmi in germany is not enough for over 198 , 00 calls if he continues answering calls 24 hours a day .
a million calls on zakaria azmi 's telephone : two years to reply and a bill of 4 million pounds
the news published by " al-gomhuria " government newspaper last thursday , concerning one million telephone calls to dr . zakaria azmi , chief of staff of the president of the republic , to check up on president mubarak 's health , stirred up widespread controversy ,
azmi denied any connection to the news release , saying that the information reported in it was " farfetched " and did not come from him , nor from anyone close to him , also noting that he did not use a mobile phone while in germany with the president .
" al-gomhuria " had said that dr . zakaria azmi " received more than one million telephone calls during his stay in germany with president mubarak to check up on the president 's health "
and that " some of the calls were from simple citizens who had searched for his mobile phone number to check up on the president " .
according to mobile phone operators that " al -masry al-youm " spoke to , receiving one million calls of one minute each through the roaming mobile system in germany , using any of the networks available there , would cost " 4 million pounds that dr . zakaria azmi would have to pay on his telephone bill if the al-gomhuria report was true " .
dr . mahmoud khalil , professor at the college of media of cairo university , considered this kind of news to be a " joke " ,
