government decides to move giza zoo to 6 th of october
newspaper reports have confirmed that the ministry of agriculture has agreed with the ministry of housing to allocate an area of 400 acres in 6 th of october city in order to move the zoo in giza to it .
official sources in the ministry of agriculture said that the agreement stipulates that the process of moving the zoo must be completed by the end of 2010 .
the sources also confirmed that it was also agreed upon that all the animals and trees will be removed from the zoo 's current location in giza , and that the current zoo 's land , which comprises nearly 80 acres , will be sold by the meter .
the sources also confirmed that it was also agreed upon that all the animals and trees will be removed from the zoo 's current location in giza , and that the current zoo 's area , which comprises nearly 80 acres , will be sold by the meter .
on his part , dr . sami taha , a member of the veterinarians ' syndicate council , said that the veterinary associations had already anticipated the matter of moving the zoo and selling its current location nearly two years ago .
taha warned about the danger of moving the zoo from its current location , as its transfer would mean the destruction of a heritage area which contains a wealth of rare animals and plants , besides the fact that the giza zoo is considered the number 1 visitors ' destination for egyptians ,
and moving it to 6 th of october means that it would only be restricted to the wealthy .
taha also indicated that the israeli embassy had previously asked the former governor of giza , dr . fathy saad , to move the zoo because they are harmed by the smells of the animals !
