surprise during investigations into the al-ayyat train collision . . the driver did not switch off the train 's automatic control device .
in an unexpected surprise in the al-ayyat train collision incident , the train 's automatic control device recorder revealed that the driver had not turned off the device , and had put the start key in a special position to respond only to red semaphore signals , and that the recorder had not registered any red signal .
accusations were made that turning off the automated control device was the principal reason for the accident which killed 18 people and injured 36 others as the device is responsible for controlling the train 's speed and cuts in to do what the driver has not done such as reduce train speed if it exceeds specified speeds , and it also stops the train in situations requiring this if the driver does not do it .
at the same time , the attorney general , abdul majid mahmoud , issued an order to speed up reports by the technical committee set up by the public prosecution office to examine evidence from the accident to decide the extent of the criminal responsibility of those involved in the accident , such as railway workers , employees and chief executives .
depending on the results of the reports , the public prosecution can summon any official - whatever their position - and question them ; they will be charged if there is definitive evidence to charge the person with causing an accident .
an on-site test , carried out on thursday at the actual site of the accident , revealed that the assyout train driver had engaged the emergency brakes manually no more than about 300 meters from the stationary fayoum train , which was not enough to prevent the accident .
abdul majid mahmoud had ordered the arrest of the driver 's assistant on the 152 al-fayoum train crash when it become apparent that he was in charge of informing various parties and the control tower in ramses that the train had stopped , but had failed to do so and this is what led to the accident happening .
engineer lutfi mansour , minister of transport , offered his resignation to president hosni mubarak , taking responsibility for the train collision , as did engineer mahmoud sami ahmed , head of egypt railways , in a knock-on effect of the train collision .
