yesterday , there was a funeral . after the funeral was over , the people brought the coffin and placed it in front of the mosque . one of the people in the area went to the mosque at 3 : 00 to pray a two bowing prayer as the late night prayer .
w started the prayer and the imam started reciting al-najm chapter . suddenly , the coffin started to move and the cover was lifted . imagine that while praying someone comes out of the coffin rubbing his eyes , yawning , looking at you and saying .
i ran out of the mosque with bare feet and the boy praying to my left ran away with bare feet . i got home in a record time and i kept reciting the two testimonies of faith all the way .
while running , the boy was saying , " what 's up , guys ! the man came out of the coffin . it 's the first time for me to pray fajr , sons of bitch . " and he continued to run with bare feet .
he looked at me and said , " the coffin is moving . " i couldn 't help but laughing . i discontinued the prayer and said to him , " what ? are you an idiot , boy ? "
he said , " have you started the prayer , sir ? " the man to my right fell to the ground out of fright .
he didn 't find the mosque attendant . he waited for some time . it was cold and he was wearing light clothes , so he opened the coffin and slept inside . i don 't know how did he dare sleep inside it ?
uncle atef , the mosque attendant arrived and opened the mosque . he also turned the glorious qur 'an station on and started to drag the coffin into the mosque alone until he placed it in its place at the qibla direction to the right .
uncle atef made the call for starting the prayer . i was unfortunate because i was standing opposite the coffin and a man in his fifties was standing to my right .
a young man of my age was to my left . the imam recited the fatiha chapter . then while saying " amen " the boy to my left noticed that the coffin was moving while he was saying the starting takbir .
once i arrived home , i closed all doors and windows and slept under the blanket and held the qur 'an book . i haven 't brought my slippers until now .
